ogin":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/4e95d5e2e640a96ae7d06205657013a512750464","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKDRlOTVkNWUyZTY0MGE5NmFlN2QwNjIwNTY1NzAxM2E1MTI3NTA0NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/b8a00dafffef965982c59bc4890389feacd9f908","sha":"b8a00dafffef965982c59bc4890389feacd9f908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/b8a00dafffef965982c59bc4890389feacd9f908"}],"sha":"4e95d5e2e640a96ae7d06205657013a512750464","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/4e95d5e2e640a96ae7d06205657013a512750464"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/b8a00dafffef965982c59bc4890389feacd9f908/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T15:00:24Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T15:00:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: register api-docs access rule and harden rule consistency (#516)\n\n* fix: register api-docs access rule and harden rule consistency\n\n- Register apiDocsAccessRules via registerCoreAccessRules so\n  api-docs.api-docs.read reaches the access-rule registry, the role\n  editor, the users-role default grant and the boot-time orphan sweep\n  (previously only wildcard admins could view the API docs)\n- Collapse pluginManagerAccess install/uninstall into a single manage\n  rule (both produced the identical qualified id\n  pluginmanager.plugin.manage)\n- Derive notification strategy accessRuleId from the emitted rule\n  (qualified {owner}.strategy.{id}.manage) and honour the admin\n  wildcard in getStrategiesForUser\n- Add repo-wide access-rule coverage guard test, update docs and the\n  generated docs index\n\n* chore: add changeset for ai-backend docs-index and pluginmanager-frontend\n\n* chore(security): remediate fixable vulnerabilities in dependency graph\n\nApplied scripts/remediate-vulns.ts against the 14 fixable findings from\nthe PR security gate:\n\n- range bumps: hono ^4.13.5, js-yaml ^4.3.2, nodemailer ^9.1.1\n- managed overrides: adm-zip ^0.6.1, astro ^7.2.8, devalue ^5.9.2,\n  sharp ^0.35.4, svgo ^4.1.0\n- lockfile refreshed; changeset bumps the affected runtime packages\n\nThe remaining unfixed adm-zip CVE-2026-76845 is warn-only (no upstream\nfix yet).\n\n* fix(script-packages): pack registry manifest sidecar into published blobs\n\nBun >= 1.4 resolves ''bun install --offline'' versions from registry\nmanifest-cache sidecars (<hash>.npm at the cache root). Blobs containing\nonly the extracted package entry dir fail host-side reconciliation with\n''no cached manifest'' - the hermetic e2e caught this on main.\n\n- resolver: bundle the package''s manifest-cache sidecar into each blob\n  (discovered by content; entry dir alone on older Bun, as before)\n- cache-archive: packEntries generalizes packDir to multiple entries\n- cache-layout: findManifestSidecars locates sidecars by package name\n- regenerate the hermetic leftpad fixture in the new blob shape\n- unit tests for the new pack/layout helpers","tree":{"sha":"20d2877d873e0301f8ab45db348abf3e4acd19c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/20d2877d873e0301f8ab45db348abf3e4acd19c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/b8a00dafffef965982c59bc4890389feacd9f908","verification":{"payload":"tree 20d2877d873e0301f8ab45db348abf3e4acd19c5\nparent 40b0bdea893cc927bf9162ef4ff86295269d4d77\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1790262024 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790262024 +0200\n\nfix: register api-docs access rule and harden rule consistency (#516)\n\n* fix: register api-docs access rule and harden rule consistency\n\n- Register apiDocsAccessRules via registerCoreAccessRules so\n  api-docs.api-docs.read reaches the access-rule registry, the role\n  editor, the users-role default grant and the boot-time orphan sweep\n  (previously only wildcard admins could view the API docs)\n- Collapse pluginManagerAccess install/uninstall into a single manage\n  rule (both produced the identical qualified id\n  pluginmanager.plugin.manage)\n- Derive notification strategy accessRuleId from the emitted rule\n  (qualified {owner}.strategy.{id}.manage) and honour the admin\n  wildcard in getStrategiesForUser\n- Add repo-wide access-rule coverage guard test, update docs and the\n  generated docs index\n\n* chore: add changeset for ai-backend docs-index and pluginmanager-frontend\n\n* chore(security): remediate fixable vulnerabilities in dependency graph\n\nApplied scripts/remediate-vulns.ts against the 14 fixable findings from\nthe PR security gate:\n\n- range bumps: hono ^4.13.5, js-yaml ^4.3.2, nodemailer ^9.1.1\n- managed overrides: adm-zip ^0.6.1, astro ^7.2.8, devalue ^5.9.2,\n  sharp ^0.35.4, svgo ^4.1.0\n- lockfile refreshed; changeset bumps the affected runtime packages\n\nThe remaining unfixed adm-zip CVE-2026-76845 is warn-only (no upstream\nfix yet).\n\n* fix(script-packages): pack registry manifest sidecar into published blobs\n\nBun >= 1.4 resolves ''bun install --offline'' versions from registry\nmanifest-cache sidecars (<hash>.npm at the cache root). Blobs containing\nonly the extracted package entry dir fail host-side reconciliation with\n''no cached manifest'' - the hermetic e2e caught this on main.\n\n- resolver: bundle the package''s manifest-cache sidecar into each blob\n  (discovered by content; entry dir alone on older Bun, as before)\n- cache-archive: packEntries generalizes packDir to multiple entries\n- cache-layout: findManifestSidecars locates sidecars by package name\n- regenerate the hermetic leftpad fixture in the new blob shape\n- unit tests for the new pack/layout helpers","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtTsICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIusQABZ9NRWCNSJ6/nojVuCve1cg\n0tF0AaNNrd+p+aMd4fHEx9mdNWA+FhtiNLWyC81eHjpbSORy0K6sEcTKtToJI2+8\n+rVqBvhuejVLiHS3Qs1HbcC20cNTCT76eOLbkt3AADGOeRnhYPlu+BmNxayUYwSn\n7XKCJJilx/tAZTI1HCwvjfElbPZkOVsTgnNkMMe0jdbLATSSndoV7rZOFh2az4dC\nwDdUJ2NNz+K4IlPJyh0rNv9ccuiU/mtfXS/9cAeLo98gz/X/ctJs0d21W4s8P7Fv\nEBnJDJc/ETFkVtTVTQXwTj6e4gnK1HtbYx8ut8yXtBDDtUpsAOj9XowHqqT9HkYB\n7tWEcascgfHE+rQWMccr3rEiWVWLEvbs3EnT2dKMIxsbElWWGIShg+seKpDQAI7j\nARDBrFff/CygpAJxwo5IBfflJJDJojHG3GhnqjcxSgOO+WkAcBpblwAX0IrBaWKh\n1708aZem45gd76XBS5SY/hcFU1LfpKoffmDSADc2/vErCR5JyU9qBD94tIO0URCq\n78EejpbPuM0aZ1+DfZIOnGSzlnvUvJDms62IRO3Vl1t60X2lkSesLbbT7K1xJJRq\nGZXMaNESCq/Hj25Xxp5YIA11fRHtKUDadL0syEXkxfdz23s3u3QEyNkI/uQ6/e2Q\ndFchOcpc