gs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/eb272fdb0d4976ef1f060c16bc17e62537172e5d","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKGViMjcyZmRiMGQ0OTc2ZWYxZjA2MGMxNmJjMTdlNjI1MzcxNzJlNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/c83d0d103ec7a5bcb1d23b4583353490b5115d40","sha":"c83d0d103ec7a5bcb1d23b4583353490b5115d40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/c83d0d103ec7a5bcb1d23b4583353490b5115d40"}],"sha":"eb272fdb0d4976ef1f060c16bc17e62537172e5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/eb272fdb0d4976ef1f060c16bc17e62537172e5d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/c83d0d103ec7a5bcb1d23b4583353490b5115d40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T20:44:03Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T20:44:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(status-page,ui): render authored markdown as blocks and colour the update timeline (#503)\n\n* fix(status-page,ui): render authored markdown as blocks and colour the update timeline\n\nOperator-authored content was drawn with the INLINE `<Markdown>`, which maps\nevery paragraph to a `<span>` and registers no heading, list, blockquote,\ntable, or code-block renderers. A structured post-mortem came out as one\nundifferentiated run of text, while the editor''s own preview (MarkdownBlock)\nhad been showing the author the correct rendering all along. Switched to\n`MarkdownBlock` on the public incident/maintenance detail pages and event\nwidgets, `StatusUpdateTimeline` in @checkstack/ui (the in-app Status Updates\nlist, edit-history snapshots too), the health-check setup guide, and API-docs\noperation descriptions.\n\nThat inline output also dragged the public timeline''s status label onto the\nmessage''s line with no gap (\"IDENTIFIEDWe found the cause\"); the label is now\na `block` with its own margin, so an entry reads status -> message -> time.\n\nThe rail dot went near-invisible between status changes: an update that\nchanged nothing drew `bg-border`. It now shows the status IN EFFECT at that\nentry, inheriting the nearest change at or before it and never a NEWER one\n(which would paint an update \"resolved\" while the incident was still being\ninvestigated). Only an entry older than every change in the published window\nfalls back to the event''s own tone. The carry-forward lives in\n`resolveEffectiveStatuses` (@checkstack/ui) and is shared: the in-app timeline\nhands each dot the status in effect as `renderDot`''s new third argument, which\na caller holding one update cannot derive, since it depends on the timeline''s\nown sort order. The argument is additive; in-app incidents already coloured\nevery dot by severity and are unchanged.\n\nThe public timeline was two near-identical copies, one in the widget renderers\nand one in the detail pages, which is how the same bugs shipped in both. It is\nnow a single `UpdatesTimeline`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0173KezbBCGuzDzGZ3q3rnyZ\n\n* fix(test-utils): register RTL cleanup at root scope so it applies to every test file\n\n`setup.ts` registers `afterEach(cleanup)` at MODULE scope. That is correct when\nthe module is PRELOADED - a preload''s hooks land at the process root and apply\nto every file - which is how `core/ui/bunfig.toml` uses it.\n\nIt silently does NOT work when a test file merely imports the setup. The module\nis evaluated once per process, so the hook is scoped to whichever file imported\nit FIRST; every later frontend file in that process runs with no cleanup and\nits renders accumulate in `document.body` for the rest of the run.\n\nCI tests each workspace package with a root-cwd `bun test <files>`, which reads\nthe ROOT bunfig - and that preloaded only the backend file. So the repo-root run\nwas exactly the configuration with no working cleanup, while\n`bun run --filter @checkstack/ui test` (package bunfig preloads the setup) and\n`bun run test` (run-tests.ts isolates .tsx files) both stayed green and masked\nit.\n\nNothing fails at the leak site; the damage lands on an unrelated file whose\nquery happens to match two elements. `Tabs.test.tsx` renders the same two tab\nlabels five times and was first to collide, failing with \"Found multiple\nelements with the role tab\" only in the repo-root run while passing on its own.\nIt fails that way on `main` today, independently of any product change.\n\nRegistering the hook from a root preload restores per-file cleanup regardless of\nimport order. Every test process loads it, so it must cost nothing without a\nDOM: the `document` check short-circuits BEFORE the dynamic import, so a backend\nprocess never pulls in react-dom or testing-library. Running alongside\n`setup.ts`''s own hook in package-scoped runs is harmless - `cleanup()` is\nidempotent.\n\ncore/ui under CI''s invocation goes from 668 pass / 4 fail to 672 pass / 0 fail,\nand CI''s full per-package loop is clean across every workspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0173KezbBCGuzDzGZ3q3rnyZ\n\n* chore(changeset): add the patch changeset for the root-scoped RTL cleanup\n\nThe coverage check flagged `@checkstack/test-utils-frontend` as having code\nchanges with no changeset entry. It is a versioned workspace package and gained\na new module, so it gets one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0173KezbBCGuzDzGZ3q3rnyZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4f4341651eb4a072079f16fcf3735e009929ba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/f4f4341651eb4a072079f16fcf3735e009929ba3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/c83d0d103ec7a5bcb1d23b4583353490b5115d40","verification":{"payload":"tree f4f4341651eb4a072079f16fcf3735e009929ba3\nparent ba9918e39346e795e38cf1c220f00d89fb43630b\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1785530643 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785530643 +0200\n\nfix(status-page,ui): render authored markdown as blocks and colour the update timeline (#503)\n\n* fix(status-page,ui): render authored markdown as blocks and colour the update timeline\n\nOperator-authored content was drawn with the INLINE `<Markdown>`, which maps\nevery paragraph to a `<span>` and registers no heading, list, blockquote,\ntable, or code-block renderers. A structured post-mortem came out as one\nundifferentiated run of text, while the editor''s own preview (MarkdownBlock)\nhad been showing the author the correct rendering all along. Switched to\n`MarkdownBlock` on the public incident/maintenance detail pages and event\nwidgets, `StatusUpdateTimeline` in @checkstack/ui (the in-app Status Updates\nlist, edit-history snapshots too), the health-check setup guide, and API-docs\noperation descriptions.\n\nThat inline output also dragged the public timeline''s status label onto the\nmessage''s line with no gap (\"IDENTIFIEDWe found the cause\"); the label is now\na `block` with its own margin, so an entry reads status -> message -> time.\n\nThe rail dot went near-invisible between status changes: an update that\nchanged nothing drew `bg-border`. It now shows the status IN EFFECT at that\nentry, inheriting the nearest change at or before it and never a NEWER one\n(which would paint an update \"resolved\" while the incident was still being\ninvestigated). Only an entry older than every change in the published window\nfalls back to the event''s own tone. The carry-forward lives in\n`resolveEffectiveStatuses` (@checkstack/ui) and is shared: the in-app timeline\nhands each dot the status in effect as `renderDot`''s new third argument, which\na caller holding one update cannot derive, since it depends on the timeline''s\nown sort order. The argument is additive; in-app incidents already coloured\nevery dot by severity and are unchanged.\n\nThe public timeline was two near-identical copies, one in the widget renderers\nand one in the detail pages, which is how the same bugs shipped in both. It is\nnow a single `UpdatesTimeline`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0173KezbBCGuzDzGZ3q3rnyZ\n\n* fix(test-utils): register RTL cleanup at root scope so it applies to every test file\n\n`setup.ts` registers `afterEach(cleanup)` at MODULE scope. That is correct when\nthe module is PRELOADED - a preload''s hooks land at the process root and apply\nto every file - which is how `core/ui/bunfig.toml` uses it.\n\nIt silently does NOT work when a test file merely imports the setup. The module\nis evaluated once per process, so the hook is scoped to whichever file imported\nit FIRST; every later frontend file in that process runs with no cleanup and\nits renders accumulate in `document.body` for the rest of the run.\n\nCI tests each workspace package with a root-cwd `bun test <files>`, which reads\nthe ROOT bunfig - and that preloaded only the backend file. So the repo-root run\nwas exactly the configuration with no working cleanup, while\n`bun run --filter @checkstack/ui test` (package bunfig preloads the setup) and\n`bun run test` (run-tests.ts isolates .tsx files) both stayed green and masked\nit.\n\nNothing fails at the leak site; the damage lands on an unrelated file whose\nquery happens to match two elements. `Tabs.test.tsx` renders the same two tab\nlabels five times and was first to collide, failing with \"Found multiple\nelements with the role tab\" only in the repo-root run while passing on its own.\nIt fails that way on `main` today, independently of any product change.\n\nRegistering the hook from a root preload restores per-file cleanup regardless of\nimport order. Every test process loads it, so it must cost nothing without a\nDOM: the `document` check short-circuits BEFORE the dynamic import, so a backend\nprocess never pulls in react-dom or testing-library. Running alongside\n`setup.ts`''s own hook in package-scoped runs is harmless - `cleanup()` is\nidempotent.\n\ncore/ui under CI''s invocation goes from 668 pass / 4 fail to 672 pass / 0 fail,\nand CI''s full per-package loop is clean across every workspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0173KezbBCGuzDzGZ3q3rnyZ\n\n* chore(changeset): add the patch changeset for the root-scoped RTL cleanup\n\nThe coverage check flagged `@checkstack/test-utils-frontend` as having code\nchanges with no changeset entry. It is a versioned workspace package and gained\na new module, so it gets one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0173KezbBCGuzDzGZ3q3rnyZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbQkTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmKEQAKkYixJgT3VvU7sRyVqo6wHB\nfx9Hiatrb+fmKd5N7hei7/dnTskYTqvsX3MaTF5JgNMgrWAMZeulqclmPzMHOgVJ\nk0ooBKYIb8xrOhfRE1eJdprD6s0Oe9kU+p+5SqYONANFWhKIfv5R1pH/iw52th0+\njD3ZmsbFYZr/aZ1ucCCXNnvjdD1xfq4flU1SKFE33MbMsFiXIiX646IwRGnwUpm1\n9SeGAv/YW89ENJonrb4ulscwuwjk2P+/euLBfJTtIkAEctELBR3rm3DsbIVEWLUO\n2gKSBqzT7q0GpRJBjnP61HhJRySSZEBCTaV5oN7Aau3eM9SY3W2rLGKcLbkBd8AI\n0nVXIufzMzVWbWM4Ep3zWjqXFrnyAOsA30w/USAYFPKCmhtg5qIgPNFqfS+p9tCv\neOAe76auyNBV4R+MUU7fK+kEu4zCdP+q2jnOQHzhnjzF5nkFE5vMaAU9AyMs0bUh\n7uiXEW+QpwnjB+hMYAPaUGHufwMYbkX7UNdYAiEk5hxnoG+ZCnD9v71/P4pPdCOb\nwJUZBnlgtBl3Vrad2Ps5l+/gQtxYKkvWdEw5N4QpSbjZbn2gaufqmfGBqoaLxD/N\nr2kQ0p1YvTyjO5iD1508ZVv/1PEVS79JppflcFFGQaBb9k/tGA2MeN5pw9U7UCYy\nkHcjQ2cjQaKuTUdnn44n\n=dxph\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-31T20:44:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web