https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/ec30265bd9bf3271c63bebb8d5bf5ff0c9bce8a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/56af5722d630b92d63854121fed9330619859d47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T11:49:43Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T11:49:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(logstream): hideable patterns, top-pattern severity filter, chart & explore fixes (#462)\n\n* fix(ui): render TimeSeriesChart at the container''s real pixel width\n\nThe chart drew into a fixed 720-unit viewBox with\npreserveAspectRatio=\"none\", so everything - including y-axis tick label\nglyphs - scaled non-uniformly to the container width. Geometry is now\nprojected at 1 viewBox unit = 1 CSS px via a new ResizeObserver-backed\nuseMeasuredWidth hook, and the SVG only renders once the width is known\nwhile the fixed-height wrapper reserves the space (no layout shift, no\nwrongly-scaled first paint). Vertical scale was already 1:1 by\nconstruction and is now pinned by a regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(ui): flash tab highlight only on actual activation (Safari)\n\nThe tab icon span transitioned `all`, re-transitioning the color it\ninherits from the already-transitioning button - a compounding lag most\nvisible in Safari; it now transitions only `transform`. Safari also\nflashed its focus ring already on mouse-down, before the click\ncommitted: mouse-driven focus is now suppressed (keyboard focus rings\nuntouched, the clicked tab is re-focused on click for arrow-key\ncontinuity) and replaced by a deliberate short-lived ring on the tab\nthat was actually activated, skipped in low-power mode. WebKit''s tap\nhighlight is disabled on the buttons.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(logstream,metricstream): stable chart states and time-bounded explore search\n\nThe explorer rebuilt its fallback \"last 24h\" range with fresh Dates on\nevery render, churning the occurrences chart''s query key: every update\nrefetched under a new key and flashed the skeleton, and expanding a log\nrow re-rendered the whole chart. The fallback window is now quantized to\nthe minute (tested pure helper), the chart keeps previous data across\nrefetches and is memoized, and all three states (skeleton/chart/empty)\nshare the 192px chart footprint - in the metric explorer too.\n\nThe default window was also only applied to the chart while searchEvents\nwent out unbounded, so filtering to a pattern fetched its ENTIRE history\nand the list could contradict the chart. The search and \"Load older\"\npagination now share the exact window the chart uses (explicit pick or\nthe quantized fallback); pagination state keys on explicit facets only\nso the rolling window never resets loaded pages. Metricstream was\naudited: all its queries already require a window or are limit-capped.\n\nAlso extracts the explorer''s severity pill row into SeverityBandPills\nfor reuse by the overview''s Top patterns card.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(logstream): keep letter-attached digits literal in pattern masking\n\nThe Drain preprocessor''s number rule masked every digit run as a\nsubstring, wildcarding constant names like S3, utf8, sha256 or TLSv1.2\n(\"TechDocs S3 router failed\" mined as \"TechDocs S<*> router failed\").\nThe rule now only fires after a non-alphanumeric separator (key=42,\ndb-9, 250ms keep masking); a digit run attached to a preceding letter,\nor continuing an identifier across a dot, stays literal - matching\nDrain3''s canonical masking boundaries. A letter-attached token that\ngenuinely varies is still generalized by the tree''s own clustering.\n\nBREAKING-ish (beta, see changeset): affected templates re-mine under new\npattern ids; user patterns authored with a letter-attached wildcard need\nre-authoring, and checks pinned to affected patterns need re-pointing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* feat(logstream): hideable patterns and severity-filterable top patterns\n\nA pattern (mined or user) can now be hidden (setPatternHidden, manage-\ngated): it leaves every default listing and its matched lines are no\nlonger stored as raw log lines - while every aggregate keeps counting\nthem (severity totals, pattern/variable buckets, spike detection, health\nchecks pinned to the pattern), so hiding fully-wildcarded noise never\nfalsifies stream volume or breaks a check. The flag lives on\nlog_patterns (append-only migration 0003); each pod''s Drain engine holds\na per-stream hidden-id set seeded at hydration and updated live through\nthe existing patterns-changed broadcast, proxied into worker-hosted\ntrees, with hydration as the convergence backstop. The Patterns tab\ngains a \"Show hidden (N)\" toggle with per-row hide/unhide, and the\noverview''s Top patterns card is severity-filterable via the shared band\npills, backed by listPatterns'' new includeHidden/bands/orderBy inputs\n(band derived in SQL exactly like bandFromSeverityNumber).\n\nState & scale: the durable truth is the log_patterns.hidden column\n(shared Postgres); reads are identical on every pod. The per-pod hidden\nset is pod-local bookkeeping over that column - same convergence\nmechanism as user-pattern clusters, never a queryable source of truth.\n\nIncludes docs for hiding + the masking-rule change, the regenerated AI\ndocs index, and integration-lane coverage run against a real Postgres.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(scripts): pin @module-federation/vite in the plugin frontend template\n\nThe template''s ^1.16 range floats to the newest release at install time\n(a scaffolded workspace has no lockfile and no minimum-release-age\ncooldown), and upstream 1.17.1 - published 80 minutes before it broke\nthis repo''s CI - regressed named-export detection for import:false\nshared subpaths (@checkstack/ui/code-editor), failing every scaffolded\nfrontend build with MISSING_EXPORT \"CodeEditor\". Pin 1.16.15 (the\nversion this repo''s own lockfile resolves; also inside the workspace\ninstall cooldown, unlike 1.16.16/1.17.0 today). Verified against the\nfull external-plugin lifecycle: 1.16.15/1.16.16/1.17.0 pass, 1.17.1\nfails. Bump deliberately once upstream fixes; Renovate does not manage\nthe .hbs templates.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(frontend,scripts): pin Module Federation exactly in host and template\n\nThis repo''s Renovate policy only runs automerged lock-file maintenance\nwithin the hand-curated package.json ranges - the caret ranges on\n@module-federation/vite (^1.16) and @module-federation/runtime (^2.5)\nmeant a broken upstream release (like today''s 1.17.1) could ride into\nthe single maintenance PR once past the release-age cooldown, fail CI\nthere, and hold every other security update hostage until untangled.\nPin both exactly (1.16.15 / 2.7.0, matching the current lockfile - no\nresolved version changes) so MF only ever moves via a deliberate edit\ngated by full CI, and add a lockstep guard test asserting the host pin\nand the scaffolded plugin template pin are the identical exact version -\nMF is the host<->remote ABI surface, so the two must move together.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"98dacdc1b9a9d45dfd475cc53f5ba317b58eef88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/98dacdc1b9a9d45dfd475cc53f5ba317b58eef88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/56af5722d630b92d63854121fed9330619859d47","verification":{"payload":"tree 98dacdc1b9a9d45dfd475cc53f5ba317b58eef88\nparent 06f11aeddb17c699b780fc309238d6a10d1595db\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1784029783 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784029783 +0200\n\nfeat(logstream): hideable patterns, top-pattern severity filter, chart & explore fixes (#462)\n\n* fix(ui): render TimeSeriesChart at the container''s real pixel width\n\nThe chart drew into a fixed 720-unit viewBox with\npreserveAspectRatio=\"none\", so everything - including y-axis tick label\nglyphs - scaled non-uniformly to the container width. Geometry is now\nprojected at 1 viewBox unit = 1 CSS px via a new ResizeObserver-backed\nuseMeasuredWidth hook, and the SVG only renders once the width is known\nwhile the fixed-height wrapper reserves the space (no layout shift, no\nwrongly-scaled first paint). Vertical scale was already 1:1 by\nconstruction and is now pinned by a regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(ui): flash tab highlight only on actual activation (Safari)\n\nThe tab icon span transitioned `all`, re-transitioning the color it\ninherits from the already-transitioning button - a compounding lag most\nvisible in Safari; it now transitions only `transform`. Safari also\nflashed its focus ring already on mouse-down, before the click\ncommitted: mouse-driven focus is now suppressed (keyboard focus rings\nuntouched, the clicked tab is re-focused on click for arrow-key\ncontinuity) and replaced by a deliberate short-lived ring on the tab\nthat was actually activated, skipped in low-power mode. WebKit''s tap\nhighlight is disabled on the buttons.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(logstream,metricstream): stable chart states and time-bounded explore search\n\nThe explorer rebuilt its fallback \"last 24h\" range with fresh Dates on\nevery render, churning the occurrences chart''s query key: every update\nrefetched under a new key and flashed the skeleton, and expanding a log\nrow re-rendered the whole chart. The fallback window is now quantized to\nthe minute (tested pure helper), the chart keeps previous data across\nrefetches and is memoized, and all three states (skeleton/chart/empty)\nshare the 192px chart footprint - in the metric explorer too.\n\nThe default window was also only applied to the chart while searchEvents\nwent out unbounded, so filtering to a pattern fetched its ENTIRE history\nand the list could contradict the chart. The search and \"Load older\"\npagination now share the exact window the chart uses (explicit pick or\nthe quantized fallback); pagination state keys on explicit facets only\nso the rolling window never resets loaded pages. Metricstream was\naudited: all its queries already require a window or are limit-capped.\n\nAlso extracts the explorer''s severity pill row into SeverityBandPills\nfor reuse by the overview''s Top patterns card.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(logstream): keep letter-attached digits literal in pattern masking\n\nThe Drain preprocessor''s number rule masked every digit run as a\nsubstring, wildcarding constant names like S3, utf8, sha256 or TLSv1.2\n(\"TechDocs S3 router failed\" mined as \"TechDocs S<*> router failed\").\nThe rule now only fires after a non-alphanumeric separator (key=42,\ndb-9, 250ms keep masking); a digit run attached to a preceding letter,\nor continuing an identifier across a dot, stays literal - matching\nDrain3''s canonical masking boundaries. A letter-attached token that\ngenuinely varies is still generalized by the tree''s own clustering.\n\nBREAKING-ish (beta, see changeset): affected templates re-mine under new\npattern ids; user patterns authored with a letter-attached wildcard need\nre-authoring, and checks pinned to affected patterns need re-pointing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* feat(logstream): hideable patterns and severity-filterable top patterns\n\nA pattern (mined or user) can now be hidden (setPatternHidden, manage-\ngated): it leaves every default listing and its matched lines are no\nlonger stored as raw log lines - while every aggregate keeps counting\nthem (severity totals, pattern/variable buckets, spike detection, health\nchecks pinned to the pattern), so hiding fully-wildcarded noise never\nfalsifies stream volume or breaks a check. The flag lives on\nlog_patterns (append-only migration 0003); each pod''s Drain engine holds\na per-stream hidden-id set seeded at hydration and updated live through\nthe existing patterns-changed broadcast, proxied into worker-hosted\ntrees, with hydration as the convergence backstop. The Patterns tab\ngains a \"Show hidden (N)\" toggle with per-row hide/unhide, and the\noverview''s Top patterns card is severity-filterable via the shared band\npills, backed by listPatterns'' new includeHidden/bands/orderBy inputs\n(band derived in SQL exactly like bandFromSeverityNumber).\n\nState & scale: the durable truth is the log_patterns.hidden column\n(shared Postgres); reads are identical on every pod. The per-pod hidden\nset is pod-local bookkeeping over that column - same convergence\nmechanism as user-pattern clusters, never a queryable source of truth.\n\nIncludes docs for hiding + the masking-rule change, the regenerated AI\ndocs index, and integration-lane coverage run against a real Postgres.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(scripts): pin @module-federation/vite in the plugin frontend template\n\nThe template''s ^1.16 range floats to the newest release at install time\n(a scaffolded workspace has no lockfile and no minimum-release-age\ncooldown), and upstream 1.17.1 - published 80 minutes before it broke\nthis repo''s CI - regressed named-export detection for import:false\nshared subpaths (@checkstack/ui/code-editor), failing every scaffolded\nfrontend build with MISSING_EXPORT \"CodeEditor\". Pin 1.16.15 (the\nversion this repo''s own lockfile resolves; also inside the workspace\ninstall cooldown, unlike 1.16.16/1.17.0 today). Verified against the\nfull external-plugin lifecycle: 1.16.15/1.16.16/1.17.0 pass, 1.17.1\nfails. Bump deliberately once upstream fixes; Renovate does not manage\nthe .hbs templates.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n* fix(frontend,scripts): pin Module Federation exactly in host and template\n\nThis repo''s Renovate policy only runs automerged lock-file maintenance\nwithin the hand-curated package.json ranges - the caret ranges on\n@module-federation/vite (^1.16) and @module-federation/runtime (^2.5)\nmeant a broken upstream release (like today''s 1.17.1) could ride into\nthe single maintenance PR once past the release-age cooldown, fail CI\nthere, and hold every other security update hostage until untangled.\nPin both exactly (1.16.15 / 2.7.0, matching the current lockfile - no\nresolved version changes) so MF only ever moves via a deliberate edit\ngated by full CI, and add a lockstep guard test asserting the host pin\nand the scaffolded plugin template pin are the identical exact version -\nMF is the host<->remote ABI surface, so the two must move together.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNFMjcLpE8iXUZHffW8voE\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqViJXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlJMQAFYZ3p0EjpUJvMnCiBdl1pSU\nWTFGvQ9/SI/Cm9Niq0F5NDnQTgMPSX+JOuqGrF+hYiTWGoYW0fVqUCRkQXR2oS0P\nD7phoYLpEpdmVunryRHxjduixCDBfBOEbadO/DxbvF1MYL9deqMbrInSG206d7Y/\nHTY2NLR7FerB4Gbf0rXmu7iJeqOfA+lDP1eqUobJ4uAT10+yz4hqrk8zZYVCedwb\n1/eEwmD+JuJ2EbJrs/7nYVLN8+KGpkcidkw+CE238qXAVFFSiQd84PK1XjFt/9xO\nd8pHXtRd+7xncukCBfYs+i0cD38+rDMIOXrEA3OT+agysEZlpvcY25qbWXuYJLLI\nPemKIdRNmZT/pbcy4CMCZ/MD4Eir6iAiopEkgFoR47m+YLxebF48hFb3jYxlkVdo\n5CKByizFRqJ7zIeSMg20JBQH3HHl5zYOUVLaODBCePkoOfyHgAHU/BpbyUoZrZMV\nnGXyVkLpvlcwL8StTUq7WXdaVR5UREXImMPW/3Mzg0X/X+XLdkkrsA0gtiiamz1k\nA0Tq+n1A6y0Bt7gMI5vH0QMIp/+GG9iYtFR7YSbF6XasCPxxIIi8k/9Ki/WswU82\nmjCkY6YhCSoAPoTBPqhYMZRHk0o7jGTd6JQpD7IOSq22ezFUz7BWjn43AnL3N7F+\nhuLNltcOULP21/xMSrnq\n=ti2/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T11:49:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url