url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/ab4680c80c63a6094fea6b0a5e0e4334ce22826d","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKGFiNDY4MGM4MGM2M2E2MDk0ZmVhNmIwYTVlMGU0MzM0Y2UyMjgyNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/654070351d04610184c1983117d8031e5768336e","sha":"654070351d04610184c1983117d8031e5768336e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/654070351d04610184c1983117d8031e5768336e"}],"sha":"ab4680c80c63a6094fea6b0a5e0e4334ce22826d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/ab4680c80c63a6094fea6b0a5e0e4334ce22826d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/654070351d04610184c1983117d8031e5768336e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:51:59Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:51:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(logstream): make the pattern-metric VariableIndex picker work (#453)\n\n* fix(logstream): make the pattern-metric VariableIndex picker work\n\nTwo combined defects left the pattern-metric collector''s VariableIndex\ndropdown permanently at \"No options available\":\n\n- The variableIndex config field never declared\n  x-depends-on: [\"patternId\"], so the editor fetched the variable\n  options exactly once at mount (before a pattern was chosen) and never\n  re-fetched. The schema now declares the dependency.\n- DynamicOptionsField assumed resolver-backed fields hold string\n  values. variableIndex is the first number/integer field with an\n  x-options-resolver: picking an option stored the string \"0\"\n  (rejected by the backend''s z.number().int()), and a stored numeric 0\n  never matched its option. FormField now passes the schema value type\n  and the field coerces in both directions.\n\nRegression tests cover the number/string round-trip, the\nsibling-driven refetch, and the schema annotation. Docs: the\nconfig-schemas guide now covers configNumber resolver fields and the\nsame-form sibling x-depends-on requirement (docs index regenerated).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DGdppnU5vbeT8XrJtAwsGB\n\n* test(ui): scope numeric-options queries to the render container\n\nCI''s full-suite parallel runner leaked the previous test''s DOM into\ndocument.body, and render()''s body-wide getByRole then matched two\ntriggers (\"Found multiple elements\"). Scope every query to the render''s\nown container via within(container) and register an explicit local\nafterEach(cleanup), so the tests are independent of which runner\ncontext (package bunfig preload vs root --parallel) they execute in.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DGdppnU5vbeT8XrJtAwsGB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70f85940bcfd69a0865ee494b490fff81109e4d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/70f85940bcfd69a0865ee494b490fff81109e4d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/654070351d04610184c1983117d8031e5768336e","verification":{"payload":"tree 70f85940bcfd69a0865ee494b490fff81109e4d5\nparent fa873e3cbe38e251233e4f0323a5c10ae3f42868\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783947119 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783947119 +0200\n\nfix(logstream): make the pattern-metric VariableIndex picker work (#453)\n\n* fix(logstream): make the pattern-metric VariableIndex picker work\n\nTwo combined defects left the pattern-metric collector''s VariableIndex\ndropdown permanently at \"No options available\":\n\n- The variableIndex config field never declared\n  x-depends-on: [\"patternId\"], so the editor fetched the variable\n  options exactly once at mount (before a pattern was chosen) and never\n  re-fetched. The schema now declares the dependency.\n- DynamicOptionsField assumed resolver-backed fields hold string\n  values. variableIndex is the first number/integer field with an\n  x-options-resolver: picking an option stored the string \"0\"\n  (rejected by the backend''s z.number().int()), and a stored numeric 0\n  never matched its option. FormField now passes the schema value type\n  and the field coerces in both directions.\n\nRegression tests cover the number/string round-trip, the\nsibling-driven refetch, and the schema annotation. Docs: the\nconfig-schemas guide now covers configNumber resolver fields and the\nsame-form sibling x-depends-on requirement (docs index regenerated).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DGdppnU5vbeT8XrJtAwsGB\n\n* test(ui): scope numeric-options queries to the render container\n\nCI''s full-suite parallel runner leaked the previous test''s DOM into\ndocument.body, and render()''s body-wide getByRole then matched two\ntriggers (\"Found multiple elements\"). Scope every query to the render''s\nown container via within(container) and register an explicit local\nafterEach(cleanup), so the tests are independent of which runner\ncontext (package bunfig preload vs root --parallel) they execute in.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DGdppnU5vbeT8XrJtAwsGB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVN9vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA240QAKP0NmGEE0P0AndLnksyt7nU\nWRnl+qLHx0y6lEy5VeAM6PTgsVKcDsxpxRbKc4Iiy6N5O0shhd9sRHhDbtW9Svd2\nM1dXQyLx43xCv22Qke9zUw5tHGThjRlu21IBgu/OG3KW5X0AlWqUKQSN2CSrq0vz\nLE6yrve1lvlNjvD/rleWNujA1rNfhGnMC2FoBDt7AXZaez9FRkjFgEIFSyesnoCQ\ny3AvUbBFCVJumh5vv6EgZ/ZTSoajZabpgxONmd5Hu7efh9cG7qVuaoAz+zLhksNQ\nI8mZoyRgHcuL23+GkFY52HusJg9Z1X9veqWr3rtyEUUk91dZhVvPGM83AbiqBpFj\nSJI0m7P7wXnjbXgnDeocRgnztD/dXYs7tK417zI70kqm/fBVi/gqDdZqbdb8xyW4\nMxpiOMTI0JQJYdMEITCysZKJrBOjw4OShI9Ftt75UeN56QvwpIomjSbORCBDoBOb\nVHsRckBPo71bxd5F5x4VgI/tdeyk9YQjxNF7zihNkFgTABon7Gw9Kn2r1X7dZEHG\ndhshQS+UD6ouWURtUln3LwESHm0idOLijiAodSPsv4uhP4qkUb2FH04FuihjWjn6\nCN2uAae3TFnVrE4fLPUNGcia/qCTlJG7YiSoGkzy9y7kPoWou02Ns/629QWuFlJg\npEIa3+CssxP/ldmYotrm\n=Bg8e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-13T12:52:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/654070351d04610184c1983117d8031e5768336e","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKDY1NDA3MDM1MWQwNDYxMDE4NGMxOTgzMTE3ZDgwMzFlNTc2ODMzNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/fa873e3cbe38e251233e4f0323a5c10ae3f42868","sha":"fa873e3cbe38e251233e4f0323a5c10ae3f42868","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/fa873e3cbe38e251233e4f0323a5c10ae3f42868"}],"sha":"654070351d04610184c1983117d8031e5768336e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/654070351d04610184c1983117d8031e5768336e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","id":29139614,"login":"renovate[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos