7?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/4568dcc7bc1da0c47e3e098e88932bb3a002bb64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T11:38:40Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T11:38:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(streams): log streams, metric streams, and satellite telemetry forwarding (#450)\n\n* feat(streams): log streams, metric streams, and satellite telemetry forwarding\n\nIntroduce two high-volume ingest stream types and let satellites forward and\nscrape telemetry on the platform''s behalf, plus supporting platform work.\n\n- Log Streams: high-throughput log ingest (OTLP + native), severity banding,\n  drain/flush pipeline, pattern metrics, protection/durability caps, and the\n  stream overview + explore UI.\n- Metric Streams: push + Prometheus-scrape ingest, cardinality caps, health\n  API, SSRF/cross-tier guards, and the metric explorer UI.\n- Satellite telemetry: a generic capability channel so satellites forward log\n  and metric telemetry and run Prometheus scrapes inside their network zone.\n  Includes the protocol foundation, agent receivers, just-in-time secret\n  delivery, binding-based authorization, and per-stream in-transit drop\n  attribution (droppedByGroup).\n- Platform: parser relocation into leaf packages (otlp-wire), ingest-utils\n  extraction, resource-scoped signal invalidation, dynamic-form row-scoped\n  option resolvers, and the ChartCard toolbar wrap fix.\n\nAll changes are captured as changesets; docs and the AI docs-index are updated\nin-tree. Verified with unit + real-Postgres integration tests and a real\ntwo-process satellite<->core end-to-end test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* fix(security): resolve CodeQL ReDoS and dynamic-dispatch findings\n\nFixes the 5 high-severity CodeQL alerts on the log/metric stream + satellite\nwork:\n\n- Bearer-token extraction (ingest-utils, logstream-common, metricstream-common):\n  replace the overlapping `^Bearer\\s+(.+)$` regex with a linear scheme-prefix\n  match + slice (polynomial ReDoS).\n- Prometheus `# TYPE`/`# HELP` parse: match through the metric name and slice\n  the remainder instead of `\\s*(.*)$` (polynomial ReDoS).\n- Satellite client capability-secret callback: store the resolver as an object\n  with a literal `settle` method so the response handler never invokes a callee\n  derived purely from the untrusted requestId (unvalidated dynamic method call).\n\nAdds a regression test covering multi-whitespace and adversarial-whitespace\nBearer inputs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* fix(satellite): align heartbeat IT test table with the satellites schema\n\nThe cross-pod heartbeat IT test hand-creates the `satellites` table instead of\nrunning migrations, and it was never updated when the telemetry work added the\n`capabilities` column. The service''s `.returning()` selects every schema column,\nso the UPDATE failed in CI with `column \"capabilities\" does not exist`. Add the\ncolumn to the test''s CREATE TABLE to match the schema.\n\nAlso add the missing changeset for `@checkstack/test-utils-frontend` (its Happy\nDOM registration was made idempotent).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3c288698ae235505168310875870ac8a50c9d54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/d3c288698ae235505168310875870ac8a50c9d54"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/4568dcc7bc1da0c47e3e098e88932bb3a002bb64","verification":{"payload":"tree d3c288698ae235505168310875870ac8a50c9d54\nparent 628352bc1497c2a5b95638a9e7d7b906bed15daa\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783942720 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783942720 +0200\n\nfeat(streams): log streams, metric streams, and satellite telemetry forwarding (#450)\n\n* feat(streams): log streams, metric streams, and satellite telemetry forwarding\n\nIntroduce two high-volume ingest stream types and let satellites forward and\nscrape telemetry on the platform''s behalf, plus supporting platform work.\n\n- Log Streams: high-throughput log ingest (OTLP + native), severity banding,\n  drain/flush pipeline, pattern metrics, protection/durability caps, and the\n  stream overview + explore UI.\n- Metric Streams: push + Prometheus-scrape ingest, cardinality caps, health\n  API, SSRF/cross-tier guards, and the metric explorer UI.\n- Satellite telemetry: a generic capability channel so satellites forward log\n  and metric telemetry and run Prometheus scrapes inside their network zone.\n  Includes the protocol foundation, agent receivers, just-in-time secret\n  delivery, binding-based authorization, and per-stream in-transit drop\n  attribution (droppedByGroup).\n- Platform: parser relocation into leaf packages (otlp-wire), ingest-utils\n  extraction, resource-scoped signal invalidation, dynamic-form row-scoped\n  option resolvers, and the ChartCard toolbar wrap fix.\n\nAll changes are captured as changesets; docs and the AI docs-index are updated\nin-tree. Verified with unit + real-Postgres integration tests and a real\ntwo-process satellite<->core end-to-end test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* fix(security): resolve CodeQL ReDoS and dynamic-dispatch findings\n\nFixes the 5 high-severity CodeQL alerts on the log/metric stream + satellite\nwork:\n\n- Bearer-token extraction (ingest-utils, logstream-common, metricstream-common):\n  replace the overlapping `^Bearer\\s+(.+)$` regex with a linear scheme-prefix\n  match + slice (polynomial ReDoS).\n- Prometheus `# TYPE`/`# HELP` parse: match through the metric name and slice\n  the remainder instead of `\\s*(.*)$` (polynomial ReDoS).\n- Satellite client capability-secret callback: store the resolver as an object\n  with a literal `settle` method so the response handler never invokes a callee\n  derived purely from the untrusted requestId (unvalidated dynamic method call).\n\nAdds a regression test covering multi-whitespace and adversarial-whitespace\nBearer inputs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* fix(satellite): align heartbeat IT test table with the satellites schema\n\nThe cross-pod heartbeat IT test hand-creates the `satellites` table instead of\nrunning migrations, and it was never updated when the telemetry work added the\n`capabilities` column. The service''s `.returning()` selects every schema column,\nso the UPDATE failed in CI with `column \"capabilities\" does not exist`. Add the\ncolumn to the test''s CREATE TABLE to match the schema.\n\nAlso add the missing changeset for `@checkstack/test-utils-frontend` (its Happy\nDOM registration was made idempotent).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVM5ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2yEQAB45cm7QURwz1dxD2zXPIsEN\nFsTQr6VQDgayCnJN+51kawJ0l9f0TROU6gv840uYAutG7udZSTLaB6Cxset1YAjZ\n32Y2YxfqeUsYflqzH72mCntjUWhT/0ykFAhxiL2HgsGTCQ44v+hAJfTOWJFjwvAF\nBsFV4PrPBrILYJaaMzguICpwmDoZ2oAAntLqD6iGnh0N6s9FF5dDSoJTArXdjTYR\nxpdTMWNjeP8ORsIc0LeVE2EtvEx7Hjog8vu5OpBX77zXSfVwsleT6XJ5xIvzgen2\neUtPZGWgKpfgzwuLYp5pWWoxRB4IROUsL9Oi51WtUpy+42Qzd2yW6B8IiEoSbscE\n2vu/SjQPJ03dZDeJ3zoO7bZgo8lIPs/jw/V6++ynjxXX+WXmXzEcDlqkgyj9vLO2\npqCpm0g2CTr/VY5I9oQHs6skB69MGkbh+qp6Pwsz8tKqglSy+MMLKKpz1zxUTHrO\ndCG5sND1ZSXTbL3ykFsFFD8Z3M5vF7aW8qkiDa6IwByelnSzM5RyDbZPY4+CFaYC\nLdsRMgsJHHVMV0Cfh8O4Blor2EuKahP3oJqRbSom7R01DrSTNKRJMZNtzlmIauR+\nfRZIU4g34C5RyEOThbplAHxZwJAV8YS7ZBvIh3NWZ1XqB2d5YbfP34Gghmuuclzc\n9uPuOanK8RhCSFbyrrgW\n=vqNe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-13T11:38:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","