":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/e8f792db07e19b52b6f0f0eb0a0f1200855a604f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T02:40:31Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T02:40:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): stop lock-file changeset from clobbering a pending refresh (#443)\n\nThe lock-file-maintenance changeset generator diffed the refreshed bun.lock\nagainst `origin/main`, but main already carries a previous refresh whose\n`Version Packages` PR has not merged yet. So the fresh diff saw only the small\nincremental delta and the single fixed-filename overwrite dropped the pending\nentries - in the worst case (empty/dev-only delta) deleting the changeset and\nCANCELLING a needed release.\n\nRead the base-branch changeset via `--pending` and union its dep list into the\nregeneration, so every still-unreleased bump is preserved and this refresh is\nchained on top. The mere presence of a pending changeset also keeps the file\nalive when the current refresh is a no-op, closing the release-cancelling hole.\n\nAlso stop fanning the frontmatter out to every reachable public prod package.\nWorkspaces publish raw source and resolve transitive deps from ranges at the\nconsumer''s install time, so a lock-file refresh changes no published artifact -\nonly the image, built --frozen-lockfile. The owner graph is now just the\nshippability gate (\"is the production image affected?\"); when it fires the\nchangeset bumps the fixed image anchors (@checkstack/backend + frontend) as the\nrebuild trigger, and the full dependency diff stays in the body as the audit\ntrail. Re-anchoring also shrinks an over-fanned pending release on the next\nregeneration.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01718H95ji4bgBqUsN5j6FYV\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"82184389385a2fcfba57eaa97344ebad830a66e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/82184389385a2fcfba57eaa97344ebad830a66e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/e8f792db07e19b52b6f0f0eb0a0f1200855a604f","verification":{"payload":"tree 82184389385a2fcfba57eaa97344ebad830a66e2\nparent a74fa0198c8f989566a921ae978a9c85356f5f35\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783824031 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783824031 +0200\n\nfix(ci): stop lock-file changeset from clobbering a pending refresh (#443)\n\nThe lock-file-maintenance changeset generator diffed the refreshed bun.lock\nagainst `origin/main`, but main already carries a previous refresh whose\n`Version Packages` PR has not merged yet. So the fresh diff saw only the small\nincremental delta and the single fixed-filename overwrite dropped the pending\nentries - in the worst case (empty/dev-only delta) deleting the changeset and\nCANCELLING a needed release.\n\nRead the base-branch changeset via `--pending` and union its dep list into the\nregeneration, so every still-unreleased bump is preserved and this refresh is\nchained on top. The mere presence of a pending changeset also keeps the file\nalive when the current refresh is a no-op, closing the release-cancelling hole.\n\nAlso stop fanning the frontmatter out to every reachable public prod package.\nWorkspaces publish raw source and resolve transitive deps from ranges at the\nconsumer''s install time, so a lock-file refresh changes no published artifact -\nonly the image, built --frozen-lockfile. The owner graph is now just the\nshippability gate (\"is the production image affected?\"); when it fires the\nchangeset bumps the fixed image anchors (@checkstack/backend + frontend) as the\nrebuild trigger, and the full dependency diff stays in the body as the audit\ntrail. Re-anchoring also shrinks an over-fanned pending release on the next\nregeneration.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01718H95ji4bgBqUsN5j6FYV\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUv6fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVekQAI5VeTzAE284jeobbqWTjEPk\nqTk4sZ6eJRZOult2PlYacbFpB/q7+gWiaT4RGLteWlkoUM1pYqIoWwQuCqnZxv/D\nxtP12TC6hWh2dMDwGoxFsECR5Xj5P7F2MVba3hH2FFJYVw3r6NXsk5pylZjublfS\nUML/4vlZNJQFQyooJ1IceXON5qGRdvGLMD58oU4p5teqYUQtvoIupfUBfuXKlJ45\nsb1TgttLt/Ug+33qUX8dMvK+KHhJ4ii7jthQktrmWPMfHWDxUjHQr7+W33MI5Vis\ntLt3TmOJyfuXCHLI/Mx6w480dJIOC1Wp6a+irP7WtuEAjBkWSC9dcm2ADILzZ1hE\nl0eX3MIqQW6nvhXBuC5APYv2wzvzAYQewqssd6IY1w03sDLivDT5TxV+7n6atwZd\namTWw8k6ruk1huVTLoHe1aUKJy9gIFHUB2pzPNX991RAe6/3qzTQrwzF4ruETEPr\nbAqty6y6bnw4JAIiTBC1+FiXsd0eJVfbixuDpAEVr3Tp6PdyY1xsdq07gFMF/RWR\n/zj7CGnwig2r/Pu1XaqTXXtWQP+TVc2IwSh4emYqeSeGKlWenQDEpFCfONRRriXp\nCx2dEhFxGiOQ2sMw+9H6ufrmiwEf9fT2ax/Wb+xgKVH04vtr/4Q90RP969qj2bDm\n+TZsr3Sxz4WJvcomRGx6\n=gBL9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-12T02:40:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/e8f792db07e19b52b6f0f0eb0a0f1200855a604f","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKGU4Zjc5MmRiMDdlMTliNTJiNmYwZjBlYjBhMGYxMjAwODU1YTYwNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/a74fa0198c8f989566a921ae978a9c85356f5f35","sha":"a74fa0198c8f989566a921ae978a9c85356f5f35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/a74fa0198c8f989566a921ae978a9c85356f5f35"}],"sha":"e8f792db07e19b52b6f0f0eb0a0f1200855a604f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/e8f792db07e19b52b6f0f0eb0a0f1200855a604f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/a74fa0198c8f989566a921ae978a9c85356f5f35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T02:16:13Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T02:16:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(healthcheck): check-centric assignment management, assertion builder redesign, and UI declutter (#442)\n\n* feat(healthcheck): manage assignments from the check editor, redesign the assertion builder\n\nAssignments were discovered and managed through a catalog system row,\ninverting how users think (\"Health Checks\", not catalog). The check\neditor''s Assignment section now owns them: per-system panels (general,\nthresholds, retention, execution, notifications, extension slots) plus\nan assign-to-system picker filtered to manageable systems. The\nsystem-centric /assignments/:systemId page is removed; the catalog row\nbutton became a wayfinding link into the system-filtered check list.\n\nBackend: new handler-authorized getConfigurationAssignments (config ->\nsystems) and a relaxed getConfiguration (readers of an assigned system),\nboth fail-closed following the history-access pattern. Route\nmanageCapability gains parentType catalog.system so pure system\nmanagers keep their assignment capability with a read-only config side.\n\nThe assertion builder now renders sentence-style rows driven by the\ncollectors'' chart annotations (labels, units, boolean prose), groups\nJSONPath under Advanced, validates incomplete rows into the editor''s\nsave blockers, and leaves persisted data byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* perf(frontend-api): memoize slot fillers to stop per-row render storms\n\nThe catalog manage page profiled as a GC-dominated main-thread storm:\nevery parent render re-ran every row''s slot fillers (rows x fillers x\nauth/query hook trees), and each useCanAccessType allocated a redundant\nsession/rules observer pair.\n\nExtensionSlot now renders each extension through a memoized component\nbailing out on shallow slot-context equality (slotContextEquals,\nregression-tested like the earlier wrapped-client cache), and\nuseTypeSurface resolves the global rule and the authenticated gate from\none useAccessRules call. A new per-row-fillers section in the\nperformance rule documents the stable-context contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* refactor(frontend): declutter entity edit dialogs into focused surfaces\n\nThe Edit System dialog stacked up to ten sections in a max-w-lg modal,\nmixing the deferred-save identity form with five self-persisting panels\nand duplicating environment membership already managed inline in the\nSystems table. Incident and Maintenance editors had the same shape,\nincluding an updates section already editable on their detail pages.\n\nDialogs now carry only what their Save button persists. The living data\nmoved to the entity detail pages behind small per-section pencils that\nopen focused single-purpose dialogs (contacts, links, team access,\ndependencies for systems; links and team access for incidents and\nmaintenances) - the detail sidebar reads identically for every visitor.\nThe redundant per-system environments picker is deleted.\n\nAlso fixes TeamAccessEditor''s transparent compact container (bordered\nbox without its own background bled the detail pages'' grid backdrop\nthrough the content; new opaque-surfaces rule in the style guide),\nSystemLinksEditor''s global-only manage gate that rendered read-only for\nteam-scoped system managers, and adds a LinksEditor hideTitle prop for\ndialog hosts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* test(e2e): drive dependency creation through the detail page''s manage dialog\n\nThe dependency editor slot moved from the Edit System dialog to the\nsystem detail page''s focused \"Manage dependencies\" dialog; the spec\nstill drove the old flow. It now follows the real user path: the\nslimmed editor''s \"system page\" wayfinding link, then the sidebar\npencil, with the editor''s own selectors unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"707424b7b072422e473b7660351fbb57a1d39347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/707424b7b072422e473b7660351fbb57a1d39347"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/a74fa0198c8f989566a921ae978a9c85356f5f35","verification":{"payload":"tree 707424b7b072422e473b7660351fbb57a1d39347\nparent d00e09930da5830ec01286cf4757e7fb0c54d262\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783822573 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783822573 +0200\n\nfeat(healthcheck): check-centric assignment management, assertion builder redesign, and UI declutter (#442)\n\n* feat(healthcheck): manage assignments from the check editor, redesign the assertion builder\n\nAssignments were discovered and managed through a catalog system row,\ninverting how users think (\"Health Checks\", not catalog). The check\neditor''s Assignment section now owns them: per-system panels (general,\nthresholds, retention, execution, notifications, extension slots) plus\nan assign-to-system picker filtered to manageable systems. The\nsystem-centric /assignments/:systemId page is removed; the catalog row\nbutton became a wayfinding link into the system-filtered check list.\n\nBackend: new handler-authorized getConfigurationAssignments (config ->\nsystems) and a relaxed getConfiguration (readers of an assigned system),\nboth fail-closed following the history-access pattern. Route\nmanageCapability gains parentType catalog.system so pure system\nmanagers keep their assignment capability with a read-only config side.\n\nThe assertion builder now renders sentence-style rows driven by the\ncollectors'' chart annotations (labels, units, boolean prose), groups\nJSONPath under Advanced, validates incomplete rows into the editor''s\nsave blockers, and leaves persisted data byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* perf(frontend-api): memoize slot fillers to stop per-row render storms\n\nThe catalog manage page profiled as a GC-dominated main-thread storm:\nevery parent render re-ran every row''s slot fillers (rows x fillers x\nauth/query hook trees), and each useCanAccessType allocated a redundant\nsession/rules observer pair.\n\nExtensionSlot now renders each extension through a memoized component\nbailing out on shallow slot-context equality (slotContextEquals,\nregression-tested like the earlier wrapped-client cache), and\nuseTypeSurface resolves the global rule and the authenticated gate from\none useAccessRules call. A new per-row-fillers section in the\nperformance rule documents the stable-context contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* refactor(frontend): declutter entity edit dialogs into focused surfaces\n\nThe Edit System dialog stacked up to ten sections in a max-w-lg modal,\nmixing the deferred-save identity form with five self-persisting panels\nand duplicating environment membership already managed inline in the\nSystems table. Incident and Maintenance editors had the same shape,\nincluding an updates section already editable on their detail pages.\n\nDialogs now carry only what their Save button persists. The living data\nmoved to the entity detail pages behind small per-section pencils that\nopen focused single-purpose dialogs (contacts, links, team access,\ndependencies for systems; links and team access for incidents and\nmaintenances) - the detail sidebar reads identically for every visitor.\nThe redundant per-system environments picker is deleted.\n\nAlso fixes TeamAccessEditor''s transparent compact container (bordered\nbox without its own background bled the detail pages'' grid backdrop\nthrough the content; new opaque-surfaces rule in the style guide),\nSystemLinksEditor''s global-only manage gate that rendered read-only for\nteam-scoped system managers, and adds a LinksEditor hideTitle prop for\ndialog hosts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* test(e2e): drive dependency creation through the detail page''s manage dialog\n\nThe dependency editor slot moved from the Edit System dialog to the\nsystem detail page''s focused \"Manage dependencies\" dialog; the spec\nstill drove the old flow. It now follows the real user path: the\nslimmed editor''s \"system page\" wayfinding link, then the sidebar\npencil, with the editor''s own selectors unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUvjtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ50QAFXt16npUuNKqG8g3KbcT19S\nBBHrg7v+qUPd5AAZRg3yXa7FXC/NIl144uggmAarcIxVfLF4AEUmi8ClWYmcpGo6\nVkAjz8Cj/VGYqs8Jdt3mN3xRGmal+gxe+qxhcs38GgAtXQ2psKmoYTH7IWGKZMo8\n+0lFOjVua21ZeuAr2NeEoBLpcLi2c6Gnk10xx5sCVjb9mSl2K3QdyZLw0+Oneb3a\nszAYJk//DYRICibU1Us7RjmsXQl1URy5fwXNIUFE29OdhzGJZlyONIpBduKFfx9R\nbCctE62khEoec93g2RJha3cDijGVrfE1kJI6MQno9kqlDAxMKnJjbjcHZaK4zo+i\nT+dw1VgY5yHwxOhpmoca5pDRxnZGRS+P+sL7HRgetHSVeJDjPbOSHJCx8F/IKqU5\nq7KDRgjI0rwDQrEqfhDLjX1npjrL199KzeLrwwuww+ySDRx/arBGDc744pdIoX3T\nVsT3ranBBhCkKJ8onyVWJvrvG34R/LiGljG0PpbLJ9EUzL/nQfnQTCnKFm8IK0pT\npsvwgWems2q2Bk+sxDBsi9ODJUbWp/A2rE1PGMluYtXjT3Axg2P9Ca+Z1LVjhBJ4\nHu0segh552YqnUIO1KokuEkbzDGy/zMg6Degqp9luozw2cM2Er9GxP4MAUhiVPzt\npBHzMlRlk40uwy2yR2TG\n=fjJa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-12T02:16:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/a74fa0198c8f989566a921ae978a9c85356f5f35","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKGE3NGZhMDE5OGM4Zjk4OTU2NmE5MjFhZTk3OGE5Yzg1MzU2ZjVmMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/d00e09930da5830ec01286cf4757e7fb0c54d262","sha":"d00e09930da5830ec01286cf4757e7fb0c54d262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/d00e09930da5830ec01286cf4757e7fb0c54d262"}],"sha":"a74fa0198c8f989566a921ae978a9c85356f5f35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/a74fa0198c8f989566a921ae978a9c85356f5f35"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/d00e09930da5830ec01286cf4757e7fb0c54d262/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T23:51:07Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T23:51:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(catalog): make System metadata usable end to end (#440)\n\n* feat(catalog): make System metadata usable end to end\n\nA catalog System''s free-form metadata (custom fields) was writable but\nconsumed by nothing: it never surfaced in templating, could not be set via\nGitOps, and had no UI editor, so models and users could not tell what it was\nfor. Mirror how Environment custom fields already work and surface it\neverywhere:\n\n- Templating: fields render as {{ system.metadata.<key> }}, namespaced so a\n  field named id/name cannot shadow the structural system.id/name. Wired\n  locally (queue-executor) and on satellites (assignment carries systemMetadata).\n- UI: System editor gains a key/value custom-fields editor, extracted into a\n  shared CustomFieldsEditor used by both the System and Environment editors.\n- GitOps: the System kind accepts optional spec.fields, replaced per reconcile.\n- Script collectors: inline TS reads context.system.metadata (SDK types\n  updated); shell collectors get one CHECKSTACK_SYSTEM_<FIELD> var per field,\n  mirroring CHECKSTACK_ENV_<FIELD>. A field mapping to a reserved name is now\n  skipped with a warning (guard added to the environment builder too).\n- Editor autocomplete/preview: offers and previews {{ system.metadata.<key> }}\n  for a concrete system.\n\nAI corrections:\n- Catalog create/update-system and create-environment tool schemas describe()\n  their metadata field so a model knows it is templating custom fields, not a\n  tagging mechanism, and sets only keys the user asks for.\n- New \"Acting on requests\" chat prompt rule: act via the tool instead of\n  deflecting to a manual GitOps/UI how-to; name the missing permission when a\n  tool is genuinely unavailable.\n\nDocs, docs index, and SDK editor bundle regenerated. No new table or migration:\nmetadata stays in catalog.systems.metadata; the satellite assignment carries a\nper-dispatch snapshot only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* chore(changesets): exclude @checkstack/sdk from changeset coverage\n\n@checkstack/sdk is generated and version-stamped from @checkstack/release\n(the SDK must never appear in a changeset, same as @checkstack/release), so\nits regenerated files should not trigger the Changeset Coverage check. Add it\nto ignoredPackages alongside @checkstack/release.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a1be7abd99700c947a94903e5f50ff638434a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/7a1be7abd99700c947a94903e5f50ff638434a9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/d00e09930da5830ec01286cf4757e7fb0c54d262","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a1be7abd99700c947a94903e5f50ff638434a9e\nparent 05827f8e3b433673513e203492c67c1896cd65fe\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783813867 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783813867 +0200\n\nfeat(catalog): make System metadata usable end to end (#440)\n\n* feat(catalog): make System metadata usable end to end\n\nA catalog System''s free-form metadata (custom fields) was writable but\nconsumed by nothing: it never surfaced in templating, could not be set via\nGitOps, and had no UI editor, so models and users could not tell what it was\nfor. Mirror how Environment custom fields already work and surface it\neverywhere:\n\n- Templating: fields render as {{ system.metadata.<key> }}, namespaced so a\n  field named id/name cannot shadow the structural system.id/name. Wired\n  locally (queue-executor) and on satellites (assignment carries systemMetadata).\n- UI: System editor gains a key/value custom-fields editor, extracted into a\n  shared CustomFieldsEditor used by both the System and Environment editors.\n- GitOps: the System kind accepts optional spec.fields, replaced per reconcile.\n- Script collectors: inline TS reads context.system.metadata (SDK types\n  updated); shell collectors get one CHECKSTACK_SYSTEM_<FIELD> var per field,\n  mirroring CHECKSTACK_ENV_<FIELD>. A field mapping to a reserved name is now\n  skipped with a warning (guard added to the environment builder too).\n- Editor autocomplete/preview: offers and previews {{ system.metadata.<key> }}\n  for a concrete system.\n\nAI corrections:\n- Catalog create/update-system and create-environment tool schemas describe()\n  their metadata field so a model knows it is templating custom fields, not a\n  tagging mechanism, and sets only keys the user asks for.\n- New \"Acting on requests\" chat prompt rule: act via the tool instead of\n  deflecting to a manual GitOps/UI how-to; name the missing permission when a\n  tool is genuinely unavailable.\n\nDocs, docs index, and SDK editor bundle regenerated. No new table or migration:\nmetadata stays in catalog.systems.metadata; the satellite assignment carries a\nper-dispatch snapshot only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n* chore(changesets): exclude @checkstack/sdk from changeset coverage\n\n@checkstack/sdk is generated and version-stamped from @checkstack/release\n(the SDK must never appear in a changeset, same as @checkstack/release), so\nits regenerated files should not trigger the Changeset Coverage check. Add it\nto ignoredPackages alongside @checkstack/release.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUtbrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyh8QACtvnrtKbHpXHujqbrAvSrSO\nMni+CUUVWnUxqJuH9/S9fUuCpk5ipapyrTO8valLIiFtP9WPQcYBDRngids7zFfi\nsXoWCb/jwQa09Kk6Dz35Kti9yyxCeWAXFpzeB7nBLeUn+XWDGfYmgOhnJA2bt706\n0kJaQxaJyrj/0uQb2x88StkmQGv2BSYow/spe5Nha13DBBhVqT6noJJzR+ZADOBn\nNpjvCJxERcEYuwYqWbUsiqge7ckWKtxRF6MifJFdxYDP/LcBzlYB9M5jMjOfSgK2\nijbCWhIKN0KYFOoZC161VTVoUEEFUb4qLz0aBI23z8IyLt1Gc01c4HRsyyIIiYMc\n9Wc3PWyXVZgwvZWF88axBO5aJhl0Z5zuHh/W00krXneOf3l909ppfBJL3KoW36ga\nXWBRBe/XXqJHObb7Gs8hq1XysMID1HPy47coTA9iukAmmsQI3qmDcP/OvuVV65Y3\nz8ZC2Qw/luELgHRaBz8piWD1wxM+8ioe3y7kkc2WokhcJ+dEcNpwlYIPUfLEZC1N\nWdANdRP2r4SR3BHtd5RzgHOF8hFXvcNmPC3tHlYd9fom+UFCEULr9JJZiCrFgF1v\nUSiqrP8ILFNLnUhkg1uEcv5W6YxckWV7Q78NJAzuIuctVpqVmsVQsAoSf9DTckWe\nOEVau4spr2d49Wxy78fG\n=DmzR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-11T23:51:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/d00e09930da5830ec01286cf4757e7fb0c54d262","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKGQwMGUwOTkzMGRhNTgzMGVjMDEyODZjZjQ3NTdlN2ZiMGM1NGQyNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/05827f8e3b433673513e203492c67c1896cd65fe","sha":"05827f8e3b433673513e203492c67c1896cd65fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/05827f8e3b433673513e203492c67c1896cd65fe"}],"sha":"d00e09930da5830ec01286cf4757e7fb0c54d262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/d00e09930da5830ec01286cf4757e7fb0c54d262"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/05827f8e3b433673513e203492c67c1896cd65fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T23:40:34Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T23:40:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cockpit): install deps from the lockfile before starting the dev instance (#438)\n\nStarting the dev instance (option 1) now reconciles node_modules with the\ncommitted lockfile before booting, so a developer who just pulled a Renovate\nlock-file refresh runs against the current dependency set instead of a stale\ntree.\n\n- install-deps.ts: installDependencies() runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile`\n  (installs exactly what bun.lock pins, never rewriting it - a plain install\n  re-serializes the lockfile on a no-op and dirties the tree). Fails loudly with\n  a drift hint if package.json is out of sync.\n- DevRunView: refactored to mirror PrPreviewView''s prepare pattern - a phase\n  machine that streams install progress, then creates + starts the supervisor\n  and lifts it to the App via onReady.\n- App: startDev() just reveals the view; the view owns prepare + start.\n\nOption 2 (PR preview) already installs its own merged worktree, so it is\nunchanged. Done in the TUI (not the `dev` npm script) so the install shows as a\nproper progress step.\n\nNote: the cockpit''s own deps must already be present for the TUI to launch, so a\nfresh clone still needs an initial `bun install`; this covers the far more common\n\"pulled a lockfile change\" case.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c3e63b8b70a0fb68c007d75938c5079851fa7ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/9c3e63b8b70a0fb68c007d75938c5079851fa7ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/05827f8e3b433673513e203492c67c1896cd65fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c3e63b8b70a0fb68c007d75938c5079851fa7ec\nparent cbf12c957895c3276d97c0c116f9cc7f9b30f8dd\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783813234 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783813234 +0200\n\nfeat(cockpit): install deps from the lockfile before starting the dev instance (#438)\n\nStarting the dev instance (option 1) now reconciles node_modules with the\ncommitted lockfile before booting, so a developer who just pulled a Renovate\nlock-file refresh runs against the current dependency set instead of a stale\ntree.\n\n- install-deps.ts: installDependencies() runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile`\n  (installs exactly what bun.lock pins, never rewriting it - a plain install\n  re-serializes the lockfile on a no-op and dirties the tree). Fails loudly with\n  a drift hint if package.json is out of sync.\n- DevRunView: refactored to mirror PrPreviewView''s prepare pattern - a phase\n  machine that streams install progress, then creates + starts the supervisor\n  and lifts it to the App via onReady.\n- App: startDev() just reveals the view; the view owns prepare + start.\n\nOption 2 (PR preview) already installs its own merged worktree, so it is\nunchanged. Done in the TUI (not the `dev` npm script) so the install shows as a\nproper progress step.\n\nNote: the cockpit''s own deps must already be present for the TUI to launch, so a\nfresh clone still needs an initial `bun install`; this covers the far more common\n\"pulled a lockfile change\" case.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUtRyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp0QQABqvMIvcsXJ86n4LSBExeI0W\ngjZmQX3UlzqQjRBrhPHdMFzbLMFBJPuhaIbTJdmQJuLKQZYugNE2c72Heepi8liV\nJC0Vbt1uanbZ9PayVAUr/0aAIFIRGXE822GvblDlBIxUr5rGHgZeCvVwrpHPKBS8\nt7dMZV/SbrF5g+gxVPWl4viha+Fve91+aZkaSCeDfpFNijF3AakubNMrvdoSpAeG\nrUCe5loc1fOpoiCAmb/XaOu6FJrf7xMC9Fa47pW0atNYlTHz6lXLbFCIrZXxQ3QK\nlbTmduNRWoeo63S3r0jo2xCoPS8sGwzU8/pCDuT2QT1xpXlmWlBCX5dbeJJijnM/\njOSLV/+oHfZe5rCU/3KO+qHGPiESCnpMTIoJMfZLgHi8G6zjfLnTztkf6eh8TWxF\nNq4tfxEJ1RIzE8tkwdaAjXzbRakoFvBKLFHPfPnGSEMcuF5Zk7SsbaqkYsuYh1Oi\nDiq+JYMtqLSCBi4A6HLgEaGQAi6xBUsxKtljnhrvAfEjcUy6Lt6YDZDIpsVZ08R4\n8yNWqeqv5SLuZ9gmnJfaMnLRoN9+yOQd2P8K6TQAVJvG0EU5r8fIS7EIQ+yK65H3\n7O+rqoyuHDKT2wFUIQJ2pjv5bPw1rS25pnFVbZJ/ebjQwS8gU0vSjDOtNYAbpdlL\n7CH0M/lAHG++ibppW2go\n=Hj2N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-11T23:40:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/05827f8e3b433673513e203492c67c1896cd65fe","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKDA1ODI3ZjhlM2I0MzM2NzM1MTNlMjAzNDkyYzY3YzE4OTZjZDY1ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/cbf12c957895c3276d97c0c116f9cc7f9b30f8dd","sha":"cbf12c957895c3276d97c0c116f9cc7f9b30f8dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/cbf12c957895c3276d97c0c116f9cc7f9b30f8dd"}],"sha":"05827f8e3b433673513e203492c67c1896cd65fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/05827f8e3b433673513e203492c67c1896cd65fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/cbf12c957895c3276d97c0c116f9cc7f9b30f8dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T22:16:00Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T22:16:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dev): predev bootstrap so the cockpit TUI can launch on a fresh clone (#439)\n\nThe cockpit is an @opentui/react TUI, so it cannot render a \"please install\"\nprompt if its own renderer isn''t installed yet - a fresh clone (no node_modules)\nwould fail to start. Add a `predev` script that ensures node_modules exists\nbefore `bun dev` launches the cockpit.\n\nIt ONLY installs when node_modules is absent; syncing to a just-pulled Renovate\nlock-file change is handled with streamed progress inside the cockpit, so this\nstays a no-op after the first install.\n\nImplemented as a bun script (scripts/ensure-deps.ts), not a shell\n`test -d ... || ...`, so it behaves identically on Windows, Linux, and macOS\n(bun runs it the same everywhere; `process.execPath` spawns the same bun binary\nwith no PATH/.exe/.cmd resolution). The install decision is a pure, tested\nfunction.\n\nNo changeset: dev-tooling change to the private root package.json + a repo-root\nscript (not part of any published package).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"edf0a133770bcec262ebddba3f71ebbb8ae50384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/edf0a133770bcec262ebddba3f71ebbb8ae50384"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/cbf12c957895c3276d97c0c116f9cc7f9b30f8dd","verification":{"payload":"tree edf0a133770bcec262ebddba3f71ebbb8ae50384\nparent 6d8bf2332ca2cfb5c5ba461343d39b07bc42222a\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783808160 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783808160 +0200\n\nfeat(dev): predev bootstrap so the cockpit TUI can launch on a fresh clone (#439)\n\nThe cockpit is an @opentui/react TUI, so it cannot render a \"please install\"\nprompt if its own renderer isn''t installed yet - a fresh clone (no node_modules)\nwould fail to start. Add a `predev` script that ensures node_modules exists\nbefore `bun dev` launches the cockpit.\n\nIt ONLY installs when node_modules is absent; syncing to a just-pulled Renovate\nlock-file change is handled with streamed progress inside the cockpit, so this\nstays a no-op after the first install.\n\nImplemented as a bun script (scripts/ensure-deps.ts), not a shell\n`test -d ... || ...`, so it behaves identically on Windows, Linux, and macOS\n(bun runs it the same everywhere; `process.execPath` spawns the same bun binary\nwith no PATH/.exe/.cmd resolution). The install decision is a pure, tested\nfunction.\n\nNo changeset: dev-tooling change to the private root package.json + a repo-root\nscript (not part of any published package).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUsCgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsjcQAE6gQuqvpA0KIhL6NCgrOS0d\n0WYYV0IyLmx/+6giIijQA4wnMuvZqt9IORRKQvobfxpRL2OP2NPeANd5posiF1cy\n6suQ1iJPcyxVA2rHWOK8CR5aCU6PS+dbV1ZlZXVAkvQYhd59y6Nh+CA9+6g609GJ\nTSO0oGsY9Yzt5NbtxaXgt74otLMQHRO+iqlfAg561+4Qx3U2roDQuKulI04I5yCq\nECCZtEBkDgL56jPXc708QKi5ieqfsvDoft5Qm7EeEixhAyLGb7Uf4RcBqzRAriHo\nFRjPcElg1BQ7X20bZHkxfzwCLReWPSCu4Vs/R/xyMwUiYB/jifGvbj3b2DimxO7l\nahiOjuMITlzeDdIarWZk7ZyxFSYz6WCsGEkW4rACK8c8XxjSnp/sLFLK0K47TBGW\nIJ/3y31uk5xfQi7cqsY65csYORE+6oG182ol3Qpn0jI7ZnFog87RdefjYMSHaNmd\n+9nBfnqq7ZCQOk2HMo3lehCEOj2Tfe8XOZlXKiLfbJ0dYkpvdaPVL4I5Xfn4+f3P\n09f6Oc5mjlJkKbOmUt9bPh7kUSKez7vKbq2EicP0qNfgD3R8B1yPfYMLEPLAQwas\nf+B5H1WOY3wSgHEf40LAGXz2KNGy04vVOYHget/6uuPj9pZlPvGCoQh/l43r5Ors\ndurNADhDPpMmBY/VGlyx\n=1d0w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-11T22:16:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com