enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/a91a1a8d00e0546d2e73e59b8b769e86877d94d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T09:15:59Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T09:15:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): let Renovate keep managing the PR after our changeset commit (#436)\n\nRenovate posted \"will not automatically rebase this PR, because it does not\nrecognize the last commit author\" on the first lock-file PR. Cause:\nrenovate-changeset.yml pushes the generated changeset as checkstack-security-bot,\nso Renovate sees a foreign last commit, assumes a human edited the PR, and stops\nauto-rebasing it. This would strand every lock-file PR the moment main moves\nahead - the automation''s core loop.\n\nAdd the bot''s email to `gitIgnoredAuthors`, the option built for exactly this:\nRenovate ignores commits from that author for edit-detection and keeps managing\nthe PR. It recreates the branch on rebase and the workflow re-adds the changeset,\nso nothing is lost. Validated with renovate-config-validator.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e08ee13dbf9d45047cf5469ecfc67b0362abce21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/e08ee13dbf9d45047cf5469ecfc67b0362abce21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/a91a1a8d00e0546d2e73e59b8b769e86877d94d3","verification":{"payload":"tree e08ee13dbf9d45047cf5469ecfc67b0362abce21\nparent b18ddcaa45a61368ad53b87fa8bdb36b904733c6\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783761359 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783761359 +0200\n\nfix(ci): let Renovate keep managing the PR after our changeset commit (#436)\n\nRenovate posted \"will not automatically rebase this PR, because it does not\nrecognize the last commit author\" on the first lock-file PR. Cause:\nrenovate-changeset.yml pushes the generated changeset as checkstack-security-bot,\nso Renovate sees a foreign last commit, assumes a human edited the PR, and stops\nauto-rebasing it. This would strand every lock-file PR the moment main moves\nahead - the automation''s core loop.\n\nAdd the bot''s email to `gitIgnoredAuthors`, the option built for exactly this:\nRenovate ignores commits from that author for edit-detection and keeps managing\nthe PR. It recreates the branch on rebase and the workflow re-adds the changeset,\nso nothing is lost. Validated with renovate-config-validator.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUgnPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZMkQAIw1q4ylqGbCGzVjwuTYhlMk\nP98EZOMcDfeMOopPMVQM0W2pL5UgiPBUqWZI/MOYfrDFb8/H5Uy4UiYSouZ3SI52\nPiOIrGULyv9NGcUWqDr1539itpqhR/u4NG9wSUikpgJ7BbPS53YIJlWbn4j1VGZh\nCb3QUb0VBuNF5khJZGhg+9ay69cPbpBKo5JMTE6c5IWY1GyAlqDhNqG2dky+Ksew\ntl+Av2iZZjVggElEeNHJQ6NaPWOcKQZcgMIsMJETu0i5Hmr11IYmbGOCmugDiJT8\nfZ+LQomNHmFfxbonLzcBpgdpanIQfhvaD2gSyxJSpOVYn4g1p7aeNIGpqQYaBbDX\nUN8Y07JCWYpujxe/oqAXsnaeTDNd1A1t/msDlyLXytXb8x1JKuxfpLCTCruggwM8\nvpbyS/FOlgU2PSPfpzGJvmfxwGDh3G8l