dZWkPXjBBgIlTw0eCFp1mSprt+oilxG218fM0sajb7vjEBKVUq\ny7Et2KUvYTdDFiH7ZGw/\n=sGYy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-10T05:30:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/509aac84577bb8d0c5a8f46af1fbceca430b1e78","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKDUwOWFhYzg0NTc3YmI4ZDBjNWE4ZjQ2YWYxZmJjZWNhNDMwYjFlNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/5e704cd8575427c5a3969b0b86a89e19c906188b","sha":"5e704cd8575427c5a3969b0b86a89e19c906188b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/5e704cd8575427c5a3969b0b86a89e19c906188b"}],"sha":"509aac84577bb8d0c5a8f46af1fbceca430b1e78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/509aac84577bb8d0c5a8f46af1fbceca430b1e78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/5e704cd8575427c5a3969b0b86a89e19c906188b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T05:27:49Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T05:27:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(frontend): de-clutter the navbar and consolidate the user-menu slot (#427)\n\nThe navbar carried six tap targets (hamburger, logo, search, help, avatar +\nchevron, bell) in a bar barely wide enough for four on mobile, and the `?` icon\nsat in the right-hand rail as a peer of the notification bell and the avatar\ndespite being neither a stateful indicator nor an identity control.\n\n- Help moves into the user menu at BOTH breakpoints, contributed by\n  tips-frontend. Its Documentation link is dropped rather than reproduced: the\n  sidebar''s Documentation group already renders a `Docs` external link on the\n  desktop rail and the mobile drawer alike. What remains (\"Show tips again\" and\n  the lightbulb/tooltip legend) are tips concepts tips-frontend already owns, so\n  the shell''s `HelpMenu` is deleted along with core/frontend''s now-unused\n  dependency on @checkstack/tips-frontend.\n- The search trigger is hidden below `md`; the mobile drawer already has a\n  \"Search...\" entry opening the same palette. Hidden with CSS, never unmounted:\n  NavbarSearch owns the palette''s open state and the Cmd-K listener that\n  `openSearchPalette()` re-dispatches into.\n- The user-menu chevron and name label drop below `md`, and the trigger''s\n  padding tightens so the tap target centres on the bare avatar.\n\nThe mobile navbar is now hamburger, logo, avatar, bell.\n\nThree defects found on the way:\n\n- `UserMenu`''s trigger had NO ACCESSIBLE NAME. The avatar is decorative and the\n  name label is hidden on small screens, so the button was announced as just\n  \"button\". It now carries an aria-label. (Found by Playwright resolving the\n  bell instead of the menu.)\n- User-menu contributions were ordered by plugin LOAD ORDER: the slot declared\n  no metadata type, though ExtensionSlot sorts on an optional `priority`. Every\n  contributor now declares one, so the menu renders Help, appearance toggles,\n  About, Logout deterministically, with Logout pinned last.\n- `UserMenuItemsSlot` had not been rendered by anything since navigation moved\n  to the sidebar - its render site was removed and the definition left behind -\n  so every real contribution went to `UserMenuItemsBottomSlot` and a \"bottom\"\n  section existed with no top section above it. The docs additionally described\n  a `group`-based grouping system for the top slot (canonical Workspace /\n  Reliability / Configuration headers, alphabetised custom groups) that was\n  NEVER IMPLEMENTED: nothing reads `metadata.group`. The two slots are collapsed\n  into `UserMenuItemsSlot`, ordering is expressed with `priority`, and the\n  fictional grouping is gone from the docs.\n\nVerified against a real booted backend via the e2e harness: navbar shot at\n320/360/390/430/767/768/1280, the mobile drawer, and the user menu on desktop +\nmobile. All six menu contributions render through the surviving slot in priority\norder.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useIsMobile()` now matches `(max-width: 767px)` instead of\n`(max-width: 640px)`, to agree with the shell''s `md` layout breakpoint. The\n641-767px range previously rendered the mobile hamburger while `useIsMobile()`\nreported false, so the chrome menus opened as desktop popovers inside a mobile\nlayout.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `UserMenuItemsBottomSlot` is removed; contribute to\n`UserMenuItemsSlot`. `UserMenuItemsMetadata` loses its never-implemented `group`\nkey and gains `priority?: number`.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7247358ec3a074b7eaa2e70f4dfbd1e4df0f66ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/7247358ec3a074b7eaa2e70f4dfbd1e4df0f66ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/5e704cd8575427c5a3969b0b86a89e19c906188b","verification":{"payload":"tree 7247358ec3a074b7eaa2e70f4dfbd1e4df0f66ac\nparent 1f20b5af09638e88e0a30b73505d605b578942ec\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783661269 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783661269 +0200\n\nfix(frontend): de-clutter the navbar and consolidate the user-menu slot (#427)\n\nThe navbar carried six tap targets (hamburger, logo, search, help, avatar +\nchevron, bell) in a bar barely wide enough for four on mobile, and the `?` icon\nsat in the right-hand rail as a peer of the notification bell and the avatar\ndespite being neither a stateful indicator nor an identity control.\n\n- Help moves into the user menu at BOTH breakpoints, contributed by\n  tips-frontend. Its Documentation link is dropped rather than reproduced: the\n  sidebar''s Documentation group already renders a `Docs` external link on the\n  desktop rail and the mobile drawer alike. What remains (\"Show tips again\" and\n  the lightbulb/tooltip legend) are tips concepts tips-frontend already owns, so\n  the shell''s `HelpMenu` is deleted along with core/frontend''s now-unused\n  dependency on @checkstack/tips-frontend.\n- The search trigger is hidden below `md`; the mobile drawer already has a\n  \"Search...\" entry opening the same palette. Hidden with CSS, never unmounted:\n  NavbarSearch owns the palette''s open state and the Cmd-K listener that\n  `openSearchPalette()` re-dispatches into.\n- The user-menu chevron and name label drop below `md`, and the trigger''s\n  padding tightens so the tap target centres on the bare avatar.\n\nThe mobile navbar is now hamburger, logo, avatar, bell.\n\nThree defects found on the way:\n\n- `UserMenu`''s trigger had NO ACCESSIBLE NAME. The avatar is decorative and the\n  name label is hidden on small screens, so the button was announced as just\n  \"button\". It now carries an aria-label. (Found by Playwright resolving the\n  bell instead of the menu.)\n- User-menu contributions were ordered by plugin LOAD ORDER: the slot declared\n  no metadata type, though ExtensionSlot sorts on an optional `priority`. Every\n  contributor now declares one, so the menu renders Help, appearance toggles,\n  About, Logout deterministically, with Logout pinned last.\n- `UserMenuItemsSlot` had not been rendered by anything since navigation moved\n  to the sidebar - its render site was removed and the definition left behind -\n  so every real contribution went to `UserMenuItemsBottomSlot` and a \"bottom\"\n  section existed with no top section above it. The docs additionally described\n  a `group`-based grouping system for the top slot (canonical Workspace /\n  Reliability / Configuration headers, alphabetised custom groups) that was\n  NEVER IMPLEMENTED: nothing reads `metadata.group`. The two slots are collapsed\n  into `UserMenuItemsSlot`, ordering is expressed with `priority`, and the\n  fictional grouping is gone from the docs.\n\nVerified against a real booted backend via the e2e harness: navbar shot at\n320/360/390/430/767/768/1280, the mobile drawer, and the user menu on desktop +\nmobile. All six menu contributions render through the surviving slot in priority\norder.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useIsMobile()` now matches `(max-width: 767px)` instead of\n`(max-width: 640px)`, to agree with the shell''s `md` layout breakpoint. The\n641-767px range previously rendered the mobile hamburger while `useIsMobile()`\nreported false, so the chrome menus opened as desktop popovers inside a mobile\nlayout.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `UserMenuItemsBottomSlot` is removed; contribute to\n`UserMenuItemsSlot`. `UserMenuItemsMetadata` loses its never-implemented `group`\nkey and gains `priority?: number`.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUILVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW9wQACRQA72uVmUrJYN+Qmj/opuD\nFb3DpMr8nM8neTrLWO5yNPQDn509SB/M3gylFMuOWhs58h86fM9uhyQfPEspFinX\nhRNKAQ+9a0KT+jMyR4+xwU3spbUIqc+ojMrF8YoPmv5TsBV2hMgJObcuQp6A43cq\ndTqzOv29dDWNHiFTv+Z+tCCs6oN9OEBerCf2T2tqYiOpdGpEg1tKWZ5dolyQZxlg\nMdJUZitoOPWNZaD3gLmaIwMprN/73KDc++1Zic/gKha/2FLphXzjdNe8rMOmPLT9\n7qoHzCbr6L2sL0rV+ReCdNPpqdWVXw6pxucq9wUf66JFY8+OXnlTkCDdfaLMw/4L\nEkTVvfmW+E4oIcBeSbAijgEV7ZVyKTsU4HKDzA6y73gHcopcYuhjsiDgiN9QbTfM\niR/oxRaPUveG9gqgUEb3DSQB93Smj9v+Km5m0rPBi6Htgx9/dlHc7bVgHW8rAN2Y\njY+fC3nj2OxP22qCLUK+OTag8kf+v6IGQ18vij1swDPzCSSofcokHQg1lb840HTy\nvoCPbYE9+tJWuLGPR9iK8G8uPHj5Pa9om6zOOoKreR8ow434JZjd/J8fHAiv2C9K\nIsMFkYSms9eERePnVHeFxb6UVsiMxu3bpLpbClDKGmA0mgN6R1S0XzXPogyUYrlr\nrmteLT80KJ0RhQ0b+Eln\n=YIex\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-10T05:27:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/5e704cd8575427c5a3969b0b86a89e19c906188b","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKDVlNzA0Y2Q4NTc1NDI3YzVhMzk2OWIwYjg2YTg5ZTE5YzkwNjE4OGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/1f20b5af09638e88e0a30b73505d605b578942ec","sha":"1f20b5af09638e88e0a30b73505d605b578942ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/1f20b5af09638e88e0a30b73505d605b578942ec"}],"sha":"5e704cd8575427c5a3969b0b86a89e19c906188b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/5e704cd8575427c5a3969b0b86a89e19c906188b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/1f20b5af09638e88e0a30b73505d605b578942ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T23:20:01Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T23:20:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(anomaly): clear a suspicious anomaly from the dashboard when it resolves (#425)\n\nA `suspicious` anomaly row that never reaches its confirmation threshold is\nDELETED rather than moved to `recovered`. Both delete paths -- the inline spike\ndetector and the hourly drift evaluator -- performed that delete silently: no\n`invalidateAnomalies()` on the router-level cache and no `ANOMALY_STATE_CHANGED`\nbroadcast, unlike every other transition around them. The frontend drops stale\ndashboard state exclusively via the signal bus (`SignalAutoInvalidator`\ninvalidates `[[pluginId]]` on any incoming signal), so nothing ever told the\ndashboard to refetch: the \"Suspicious behaviour\" badge, the system-detail widget\nand the aggregated system signal stayed on screen until an incidental refetch\n(remount or window refocus) happened to fire.\n\nBoth delete branches now drop the cache and broadcast, so the badge disappears\nas soon as the metric returns to normal.\n\nThe drift evaluator additionally never invalidated the router cache on ANY of\nits writes (create / confirm / self-resolve / recover), so a forced refetch could\nstill read a stale anomaly list back out of the 15s server-side cache. It now\ninvalidates on every row write, matching the spike detector. To make that\npossible the router cache is constructed before the baseline-analyzer job is\nscheduled and threaded into `evaluateDrift`.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `ANOMALY_STATE_CHANGED`''s `newState` is now typed by the new\n`AnomalyStateChangeSchema` (`suspicious` | `anomaly` | `recovered` | `cleared`)\nrather than the persisted `AnomalyStateSchema`. The added `cleared` value marks\n\"an unconfirmed suspicious row was deleted\", which has no persisted state to\nreport. It is deliberately distinct from `recovered`: a suspicious row never\nproduced a \"confirmed\" notification, so clearing it must not look like a\nrecovery to a subscriber that alerts on one.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca01b6ee6cd6d148b50a3c05c322af8a0b954c01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/ca01b6ee6cd6d148b50a3c05c322af8a0b954c01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/1f20b5af09638e88e0a30b73505d605b578942ec","verification":{"payload":"tree ca01b6ee6cd6d148b50a3c05c322af8a0b954c01\nparent 18fbae5d991c187efe771e007754a84a4f6b60e4\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783639201 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783639201 +0200\n\nfix(anomaly): clear a suspicious anomaly from the dashboard when it resolves (#425)\n\nA `suspicious` anomaly row that never reaches its confirmation threshold is\nDELETED rather than moved to `recovered`. Both delete paths -- the inline spike\ndetector and the hourly drift evaluator -- performed that delete silently: no\n`invalidateAnomalies()` on the router-level cache and no `ANOMALY_STATE_CHANGED`\nbroadcast, unlike every other transition around them. The frontend drops stale\ndashboard state exclusively via the signal bus (`SignalAutoInvalidator`\ninvalidates `[[pluginId]]` on any incoming signal), so nothing ever told the\ndashboard to refetch: the \"Suspicious behaviour\" badge, the system-detail widget\nand the aggregated system signal stayed on screen until an incidental refetch\n(remount or window refocus) happened to fire.\n\nBoth delete branches now drop the cache and broadcast, so the badge disappears\nas soon as the metric returns to normal.\n\nThe drift evaluator additionally never invalidated the router cache on ANY of\nits writes (create / confirm / self-resolve / recover), so a forced refetch could\nstill read a stale anomaly list back out of the 15s server-side cache. It now\ninvalidates on every row write, matching the spike detector. To make that\npossible the router cache is constructed before the baseline-analyzer job is\nscheduled and threaded into `evaluateDrift`.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `ANOMALY_STATE_CHANGED`''s `newState` is now typed by the new\n`AnomalyStateChangeSchema` (`suspicious` | `anomaly` | `recovered` | `cleared`)\nrather than the persisted `AnomalyStateSchema`. The added `cleared` value marks\n\"an unconfirmed suspicious row was deleted\", which has no persisted state to\nreport. It is deliberately distinct from `recovered`: a suspicious row never\nproduced a \"confirmed\" notification, so clearing it must not look like a\nrecovery to a subscriber that alerts on one.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gj1eu1Q46UAZT3Z79K2E1N\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUCyhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACawQAGR3wHe0eq97yMqP1EVJubBq\nJqk1C+xNGKB8l7QlrlHi2kPOLdGKoMaVDFi7c4kkTP+Jcl/Te5tDxj2C170lzst5\nZ5n3VyBn5N6X4g4nORocQ7GHyUtPb1JKVyMd1D8UimC6lD6CfmHRe71oh2ZyIw2Y\nbPIwuPKuTQGUNwbfNR5sUgV3pHb6VEI93yYZrPzKtOfIfb9GvpIJF+mSznL2j221\nECPnUEN+7ii7bq5HqF0wqVTgcuCZvaQ2WUU9yzC4UT/0KX6n6Mk7ya6KS12z758j\nI7QpclDR40h6Ch3/hjr1BsjHRxS3ZUebxPGEr1aegLwQItgYzqTKSlWEoD0ZaeAJ\n6SV0+OdfrdBddYUB+a0O0vFggxVk/pGUsPeFt6gDI1PlTj4Y3GD3bBb5Vn9I+lIr\nsVoL9zwSY/KJC5gRky/oMOJRyXyCBqdOyFUMikbWE9Gb5/hymNzTLLT5scaGy0jH\nVBsPrt9EXMAhSCBXiNcOr51TNyDOojz/FmRsYoP9+tJo2/9SZL/DkF31XehTq/Ar\njYX+aJmYYUdH1cWgi/nV43Wi97USJTRL/9n9KyS5EYdOr8v7P7GJiw4g7M2cyIFO\nE68hSOx8otZ3mgRq5xL5g+TFZRMSXSWrZ8Mcfxze4bk1cy/PFYzGVRV3cgM7g2qz\nNbs9ogRf7WYkgQEf8Q3V\n=5lgy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T23:20:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatar