","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/b80160a08939e9df26e5aee237c1afe0b5736bdf"}],"sha":"18fbae5d991c187efe771e007754a84a4f6b60e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/18fbae5d991c187efe771e007754a84a4f6b60e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/b80160a08939e9df26e5aee237c1afe0b5736bdf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:40:49Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:40:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(frontend): kill the catalog-manager render/query storm (#424)\n\nNavigating to the catalog manager blocked the main thread. Two causes, both\nmultiplied by the team-scoped RLAC gating added to every per-system surface:\n\n1. usePluginClient rebuilt the whole wrapped plugin client (one hook-wrapper\n   closure per contract procedure - ~80 for AuthApi) PER COMPONENT INSTANCE.\n   Every auth-gated badge/action per row rebuilt it, so a page rebuilt it ~8x\n   per row - a synchronous closure/GC storm on navigation. The wrappers are\n   render-agnostic, so the wrapped client is now cached in a module WeakMap\n   keyed on the stable (pluginUtils, contract) and built ONCE per plugin,\n   shared by every caller. O(instances x procedures) -> O(plugins x procedures).\n   Covered by orpc-client-cache.test.ts.\n\n2. SystemHealthCheckAssignment (per-row catalog action) gated on a single-id\n   useResourceAccess({ resourceIds: [systemId] }), so N rows fired N distinct\n   listMyAccessibleResources queries (keys differ, no dedupe). It now passes the\n   visibleSystemIds it already receives, so every row''s identical-input query\n   dedupes to ONE request and the row still gates on canAccess(systemId) - the\n   same pattern the file''s getBulkAssignedHealthCheckCounts query already uses.\n\nA frontend-wide audit confirmed these were the only two instances of these\nclasses; every other per-row surface already batches (bulk data-provider slots,\n.map()-lifted gates, getBulk* endpoints).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b7c24f08142ef4384971e332fea187210d9ee0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/3b7c24f08142ef4384971e332fea187210d9ee0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/b80160a08939e9df26e5aee237c1afe0b5736bdf","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b7c24f08142ef4384971e332fea187210d9ee0c\nparent bd411304814b8f1665046c36d2ab8556b2e7acd3\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783615249 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783615249 +0200\n\nperf(frontend): kill the catalog-manager render/query storm (#424)\n\nNavigating to the catalog manager blocked the main thread. Two causes, both\nmultiplied by the team-scoped RLAC gating added to every per-system surface:\n\n1. usePluginClient rebuilt the whole wrapped plugin client (one hook-wrapper\n   closure per contract procedure - ~80 for AuthApi) PER COMPONENT INSTANCE.\n   Every auth-gated badge/action per row rebuilt it, so a page rebuilt it ~8x\n   per row - a synchronous closure/GC storm on navigation. The wrappers are\n   render-agnostic, so the wrapped client is now cached in a module WeakMap\n   keyed on the stable (pluginUtils, contract) and built ONCE per plugin,\n   shared by every caller. O(instances x procedures) -> O(plugins x procedures).\n   Covered by orpc-client-cache.test.ts.\n\n2. SystemHealthCheckAssignment (per-row catalog action) gated on a single-id\n   useResourceAccess({ resourceIds: [systemId] }), so N rows fired N distinct\n   listMyAccessibleResources queries (keys differ, no dedupe). It now passes the\n   visibleSystemIds it already receives, so every row''s identical-input query\n   dedupes to ONE request and the row still gates on canAccess(systemId) - the\n   same pattern the file''s getBulkAssignedHealthCheckCounts query already uses.\n\nA frontend-wide audit confirmed these were the only two instances of these\nclasses; every other per-row surface already batches (bulk data-provider slots,\n.map()-lifted gates, getBulk* endpoints).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT88RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASYsQAEHHlp4lLN4PfiT3qW0NdYnc\nh4bRAlaj/rH2/raveGCKIa2rIPHkb7PFmqBKOf9n4rO4YLQ9hLWAW/Ft74qtzBcG\nW8OLEqHTL+bZcGzAp9vxdboVffbhvcOrB4iCOUtKkjbA4qgVqp02tGa96fEefopp\nI3urTRkkolDfB+H0IG28HqxcdozprfpP6DOM6ndshei9U/rGfDZrvuARorctDl2A\n32HmTv30vTPGoUwd8b6wJIncZNz7Zx9WcjwIEXc+vwbIzEcY/XyaDZ9uzEl28ZLH\nMYbbTutw/a3RFKgI7I358Y8/ZNyxFEW+rZ1BHcie1/5ZShrGWiSFRf8rFT6L+HxF\nqJNT0yqHxjZFUjNJqMz0pzkjOZymPDs16WUdeoX8dNCPZXWuPbndnWe5Z7J7SmSz\ni8CDbNLa+nWC+fxKaD8lNXp9mmjpp0FlRFd/KCRPUDYQJk8XPJPWcEEdGfkMC3tJ\natAosA4SopRiYLeQdesCeljHKBl+9KHXBFwlq29DjbiwqsnSiscwQloG6zilrp0y\n+pMYHS7885PnT+wCBxyHz4+aDk28fWb3V/cwiYsmvBdRfgrCTodAh0YlEOcapRRE\n4mi6ZcXSxPtOmgJpNGnRBcEyuw5YgIAIcqCdZwmt0Xz05ynlLFeFdP5oACqeiBWI\nlcpTUKG+N3iVXBzsZi8A\n=QFb8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T16:40:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/b80160a08939e9df26e5aee237c1afe0b5736bdf","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKGI4MDE2MGEwODkzOWU5ZGYyNmU1YWVlMjM3YzFhZmUwYjU3MzZiZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/bd411304814b8f1665046c36d2ab8556b2e7acd3","sha":"bd411304814b8f1665046c36d2ab8556b2e7acd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/bd411304814b8f1665046c36d2ab8556b2e7acd3"}],"sha":"b80160a08939e9df26e5aee237c1afe0b5736bdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/b80160a08939e9df26e5aee237c1afe0b5736bdf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/bd411304814b8f1665046c36d2ab8556b2e7acd3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:47:50Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:47:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: distributed read-path caching, hot-path indexes, and related hardening (#422)\n\n* perf: distributed read-path caching, hot-path indexes, and related hardening\n\nMigrate the auth and healthcheck read-path caches off per-pod TTL caches\n(kept coherent by an application broadcast) onto the platform''s shared\ndistributed CacheManager, so a load-balanced request gets an up-to-date\nauthorization/health answer on any pod.\n\nCaching:\n- New @checkstack/cache-redis-backend provider (v8 serialize/deserialize,\n  namespaced per instance) so the shared cache is coherent across pods.\n- Auth: cache user->roles and role->access-rule ids read-through, plus the\n  anonymous role''s effective rules; reads are cache-first and outside any DB\n  transaction. All writes funnel through RoleMembershipStore, which welds each\n  write to its cache delete; access-rule-sync evicts affected shared entries on\n  boot fullSync when a default-rule change actually mutates grants.\n- Healthcheck: status cache keyed per (system, environment), change-gated on the\n  per-check status vector; env-scoped change evicts the env + rollup keys.\n- cache-utils: add CachedScope.wrapManyBatched (epoch-guarded batched\n  read-through) so the batched role-rules load keeps the single-key staleness\n  guarantee.\n- JWT keystore cached and pruned.\n\nIndexes: add hot-path database indexes across 9 backends (anomaly, slo,\nhealthcheck, incident, maintenance, dependency, catalog, notification,\nstatus-page), each as an append-only migration + changeset.\n\nAlso: env-scoped health subscriptions (status-page), catalog bulk\nhealth-badge management, healthcheck executor deferral of rollup recompute,\nand an Alert icon-shrink fix.\n\nDocs and the AI docs-index are updated to match; a new optimization rule\ndocuments preferring the shared distributed cache over pod-local caches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(ci): resolve integration, security, and e2e failures\n\nThree CI failures surfaced by checks that the local `bun test` cannot run\n(integration + e2e need Postgres/Redis/a built frontend):\n\n- Integration: the status-page subscriber fan-out test''s stub widget lacked a\n  `subscriptionCategory`, so the new per-category fan-out gate (which only\n  surfaces a widget whose category matches the notification''s source) dropped it\n  and notifyForSystems returned 0. The stub now declares `subscriptionCategory:\n  \"incident\"`, matching the sole fan-out test''s incident source, so it faithfully\n  represents a real incident feed widget. Verified against real Postgres (20/20).\n\n- Security (Trivy): the new ioredis-mock dev dependency pulls fengari, which pins\n  tmp ^0.2.5; the resolver hoisted the vulnerable tmp 0.2.5 (CVE-2026-44705,\n  HIGH) to top-level. fengari accepts ^0.2.5, so pin tmp to the already-present\n  0.2.7 via overrides/resolutions and document it in security/managed-overrides\n  .json. `audit:overrides:check` passes; no tmp 0.2.5 remains in the lockfile.\n\n- E2E: the in-memory cache warning title was strengthened to \"In-memory cache:\n  single instance only\"; the cache.spec assertion still looked for the old\n  \"In-Memory Cache Warning\" exact text. Updated to the new copy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* refactor(cache-redis): drop ioredis-mock; test RedisCache against real Redis\n\nThe RedisCache unit test swapped in `ioredis-mock`, which pulls `fengari` (a\nfull Lua VM in JS, to emulate Redis EVAL) plus `fengari-interop` - a large\ntransitive surface for a test mock, and the source of the tmp CVE the previous\ncommit had to pin around. A mock also can only prove we CALL the right commands,\nnever that Redis behaves as RedisCache assumes (Buffer vs string from getBuffer,\nPX TTL semantics, SCAN cursor paging, UNLINK).\n\n- Convert redis-cache.test.ts -> redis-cache.it.test.ts: same cases, now run\n  against a real Redis (CHECKSTACK_IT-gated, CHECKSTACK_IT_REDIS_URL), mirroring\n  the existing bullmq-queue.it.test.ts pattern. Keys are namespaced per run and\n  purged after each test so a persistent Redis stays hermetic. Verified: 7/7\n  against real Redis; correctly skipped in bare `bun test`.\n- Remove the `ioredis-mock` devDependency from cache-redis-backend, and from\n  queue-bullmq-backend where it was declared but never imported (dead dep).\n- Remove the now-unnecessary ioredis-mock.d.ts type shim.\n- Drop the `tmp` override (package.json overrides/resolutions + managed-overrides\n  .json): with fengari gone, the only tmp consumer is testcontainers, which\n  already resolves the safe 0.2.7. Verified no ioredis-mock/fengari entries and\n  no tmp 0.2.5 remain in the lockfile; audit:overrides:check passes.\n\nNote: the \"51 weekly downloads\" concern was a different package - the real\nioredis-mock is ~1.5M/week, MIT, maintained. We drop it anyway to shed the\nfengari transitive surface and test the provider against the thing it wraps.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* docs(changeset): cover cache-frontend, test-utils-backend, queue-bullmq-backend\n\nThe changeset-coverage check flagged three published packages with non-test\nchanges that no changeset named:\n\n- @checkstack/cache-frontend: the strengthened in-memory cache warning copy.\n- @checkstack/test-utils-backend: the new lockPool on the mock DB module.\n- @checkstack/queue-bullmq-backend: dropping the unused ioredis-mock devDep.\n\nEach gets a focused patch changeset (platform is BETA; none are breaking).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3fb4fdd6897ebae2ec652a74295226c6de681b36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/3fb4fdd6897ebae2ec652a74295226c6de681b36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/bd411304814b8f1665046c36d2ab8556b2e7acd3","verification":{"payload":"tree 3fb4fdd6897ebae2ec652a74295226c6de681b36\nparent 6b6779393212855030dc8de2756305597db021eb\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783612070 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783612070 +0200\n\nperf: distributed read-path caching, hot-path indexes, and related hardening (#422)\n\n* perf: distributed read-path caching, hot-path indexes, and related hardening\n\nMigrate the auth and healthcheck read-path caches off per-pod TTL caches\n(kept coherent by an application broadcast) onto the platform''s shared\ndistributed CacheManager, so a load-balanced request gets an up-to-date\nauthorization/health answer on any pod.\n\nCaching:\n- New @checkstack/cache-redis-backend provider (v8 serialize/deserialize,\n  namespaced per instance) so the shared cache is coherent across pods.\n- Auth: cache user->roles and role->access-rule ids read-through, plus the\n  anonymous role''s effective rules; reads are cache-first and outside any DB\n  transaction. All writes funnel through RoleMembershipStore, which welds each\n  write to its cache delete; access-rule-sync evicts affected shared entries on\n  boot fullSync when a default-rule change actually mutates grants.\n- Healthcheck: status cache keyed per (system, environment), change-gated on the\n  per-check status vector; env-scoped change evicts the env + rollup keys.\n- cache-utils: add CachedScope.wrapManyBatched (epoch-guarded batched\n  read-through) so the batched role-rules load keeps the single-key staleness\n  guarantee.\n- JWT keystore cached and pruned.\n\nIndexes: add hot-path database indexes across 9 backends (anomaly, slo,\nhealthcheck, incident, maintenance, dependency, catalog, notification,\nstatus-page), each as an append-only migration + changeset.\n\nAlso: env-scoped health subscriptions (status-page), catalog bulk\nhealth-badge management, healthcheck executor deferral of rollup recompute,\nand an Alert icon-shrink fix.\n\nDocs and the AI docs-index are updated to match; a new optimization rule\ndocuments preferring the shared distributed cache over pod-local caches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(ci): resolve integration, security, and e2e failures\n\nThree CI failures surfaced by checks that the local `bun test` cannot run\n(integration + e2e need Postgres/Redis/a built frontend):\n\n- Integration: the status-page subscriber fan-out test''s stub widget lacked a\n  `subscriptionCategory`, so the new per-category fan-out gate (which only\n  surfaces a widget whose category matches the notification''s source) dropped it\n  and notifyForSystems returned 0. The stub now declares `subscriptionCategory:\n  \"incident\"`, matching the sole fan-out test''s incident source, so it faithfully\n  represents a real incident feed widget. Verified against real Postgres (20/20).\n\n- Security (Trivy): the new ioredis-mock dev dependency pulls fengari, which pins\n  tmp ^0.2.5; the resolver hoisted the vulnerable tmp 0.2.5 (CVE-2026-44705,\n  HIGH) to top-level. fengari accepts ^0.2.5, so pin tmp to the already-present\n  0.2.7 via overrides/resolutions and document it in security/managed-overrides\n  .json. `audit:overrides:check` passes; no tmp 0.2.5 remains in the lockfile.\n\n- E2E: the in-memory cache warning title was strengthened to \"In-memory cache:\n  single instance only\"; the cache.spec assertion still looked for the old\n  \"In-Memory Cache Warning\" exact text. Updated to the new copy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* refactor(cache-redis): drop ioredis-mock; test RedisCache against real Redis\n\nThe RedisCache unit test swapped in `ioredis-mock`, which pulls `fengari` (a\nfull Lua VM in JS, to emulate Redis EVAL) plus `fengari-interop` - a large\ntransitive surface for a test mock, and the source of the tmp CVE the previous\ncommit had to pin around. A mock also can only prove we CALL the right commands,\nnever that Redis behaves as RedisCache assumes (Buffer vs string from getBuffer,\nPX TTL semantics, SCAN cursor paging, UNLINK).\n\n- Convert redis-cache.test.ts -> redis-cache.it.test.ts: same cases, now run\n  against a real Redis (CHECKSTACK_IT-gated, CHECKSTACK_IT_REDIS_URL), mirroring\n  the existing bullmq-queue.it.test.ts pattern. Keys are namespaced per run and\n  purged after each test so a persistent Redis stays hermetic. Verified: 7/7\n  against real Redis; correctly skipped in bare `bun test`.\n- Remove the `ioredis-mock` devDependency from cache-redis-backend, and from\n  queue-bullmq-backend where it was declared but never imported (dead dep).\n- Remove the now-unnecessary ioredis-mock.d.ts type shim.\n- Drop the `tmp` override (package.json overrides/resolutions + managed-overrides\n  .json): with fengari gone, the only tmp consumer is testcontainers, which\n  already resolves the safe 0.2.7. Verified no ioredis-mock/fengari entries and\n  no tmp 0.2.5 remain in the lockfile; audit:overrides:check passes.\n\nNote: the \"51 weekly downloads\" concern was a different package - the real\nioredis-mock is ~1.5M/week, MIT, maintained. We drop it anyway to shed the\nfengari transitive surface and test the provider against the thing it wraps.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* docs(changeset): cover cache-frontend, test-utils-backend, queue-bullmq-backend\n\nThe changeset-coverage check flagged three published packages with non-test\nchanges that no changeset named:\n\n- @checkstack/cache-frontend: the strengthened in-memory cache warning copy.\n- @checkstack/test-utils-backend: the new lockPool on the mock DB module.\n- @checkstack/queue-bullmq-backend: dropping the unused ioredis-mock devDep.\n\nEach gets a focused patch changeset (platform is BETA; none are breaking).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT8KmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArn0QAJZsffBmNDrw1A6vu1VmApiF\nQUyk3AT9v70OxfVWgs7q9r9yA8p7XzhQIadbAMuFPEm64VepBfbGXroynBR3RZu6\nYvQNO/eWvFNuuf/TCd7WIn82iW0Oifrwb3yYjxH7LNLFr8oWiBbWL99LqPzZ24LN\ndz6rBmS3yPHRhAqdA4lzHxi3spsga5j7EUlQC4S05hGeF/gdgilnMDmWQnzCmwAt\nNUQOsRjtyB/4PS167zbhr1bskGQoMWGyXyRz0/S8Ci52PKwgzEH65qMc0EkNiJP3\nNKegC+6AgW/RJocKZmHqd1BzmbI68EZOsTFBiH54kWSAZElm9eQPJAZXcKgSjt4w\nNGKznHPxpCSjtd+oF6J+