hub.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/6b6779393212855030dc8de2756305597db021eb","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKDZiNjc3OTM5MzIxMjg1NTAzMGRjOGRlMjc1NjMwNTU5N2RiMDIxZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/43e448440abbdca9e01eb95944f9312a7c108d62","sha":"43e448440abbdca9e01eb95944f9312a7c108d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/43e448440abbdca9e01eb95944f9312a7c108d62"}],"sha":"6b6779393212855030dc8de2756305597db021eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/6b6779393212855030dc8de2756305597db021eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/43e448440abbdca9e01eb95944f9312a7c108d62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T05:55:53Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T05:55:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Beta feedback, performance, and status-page/SLO features (#420)\n\n* feat: beta feedback fixes, N+1/perf optimizations, and query profiler\n\nA large checkpoint batch spanning user-feedback fixes (from @stuajnht''s\nbeta feedback), performance/N+1 work, observability, and a docs build fix.\n39 changesets; see each for scope. Highlights:\n\nUser feedback (features & bugfixes)\n- Health checks: SNMP strategy/collector; environment templating extended\n  across every built-in check type (+ SNMP host/OID, script cwd; script\n  bodies intentionally not templatable); fix HTTP 400 when opening Anomaly\n  Defaults on an unsaved check; clarified \"connect a satellite\" assignment\n  docs.\n- Status pages: custom-domain pages load (skip cross-origin /api/config\n  probe; CORS admits verified domains); group widgets collapse-when-healthy;\n  incident/maintenance deep links + minimal custom-domain router; anonymous\n  email subscriptions (double opt-in) + admin list/remove; group-scoped\n  incident/maintenance widgets; announcements widget.\n- Incidents/maintenance: Markdown; edit/delete updates + published-time edit\n  + manager-only edit history; three-way update visibility\n  (public/logged_in/internal); \"Keep Current (status)\"; internal notes;\n  logged-out overview pages + nav; fix grey `minor`/`monitoring` status\n  colours (app + status page); editable hotlinks (incident/maintenance/\n  catalog system links).\n- Notifications: latest update text in the body (incident + maintenance);\n  name the failing health check; generic outgoing webhook channel (with\n  SSRF/egress guard); \"Your Subscriptions\" moved to its own page.\n- Misc: API-docs examples use BASE_URL from the OpenAPI server; edit\n  satellite name/region without touching the token; catalog group sort\n  order; SLO error budget can exclude scheduled maintenance windows.\n\nPerformance / N+1\n- Catalog browse: bulk-data boundary slot removes per-row health/incident/\n  maintenance/SLO/dependency/subscription N+1s.\n- Status-page widgets: bulk-by-id resolvers (getBulkRunStats, bulk update\n  fetches) replace per-item RPC fan-out.\n- Backends: batched anomaly/notification/automation reads; scoped-db\n  transaction batching across catalog/slo/automation/dependency and remaining\n  backends; maintenance cron transition batched; secrets resolve active\n  backend once per batch.\n- Frontend: coalesce realtime signal invalidations to stop health-status\n  refetch storms.\n\nObservability\n- DB query/transaction duration histograms + pg_stat_statements export\n  (opt-in via CHECKSTACK_METRICS_ENABLED); profiling analyzer script under\n  core/scripts.\n\nBuild/tooling\n- Fix docs build warning by deduping @astrojs/markdown-remark to ^7.2.0\n  (astro-mermaid resolved a stale copy lacking isUnifiedProcessor).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(healthcheck-script): transport-only success/error aggregate tiles\n\nThe Script strategy''s mergeResult read the pre-collector per-run shape\n(metadata.success/executionTimeMs/timedOut), which is undefined in the\ncollector-based model, so Success Rate and Avg Execution Time tiles read\n0% / 0ms while per-run charts were correct. It then briefly used run.status,\nwhich conflates assertion failures with genuine errors.\n\nDerive the aggregates from the run''s transport signals stored under\nmetadata.collectors[<id>] (_collectorError, timedOut) plus a top-level error,\nmatching every other strategy and .claude/rules/healthcheck-collectors.md:\nSuccess Rate and Errors reflect only whether the probe completed, independent\nof assertion outcomes. avgExecutionTime uses run.latencyMs. Assertion failures\n(_assertionFailed) no longer lower Success Rate or count as Errors; they remain\nvisible as unhealthy in the health timeline.\n\nAdds real-shape regression tests: assertion-failure-is-not-an-error, genuine\ntransport error counts, and timeout counts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(catalog): consistent card design for incidents and SLO overview panels\n\nThe \"active incidents\" and \"SLO\" panels on the system overview rendered as thin\nrounded-md banner strips, inconsistent with the maintenance, dependencies,\nhealth-checks and anomaly cards. Restyle both to the shared card recipe\n(rounded-[var(--d-card-r)], from-surface-2/to-surface gradient, p-[var(--d-pad)],\nshared panel shadow).\n\n- Incidents match the sibling maintenance banner: status-colored left accent,\n  large count + caption, severity pills preserved; loading/empty states updated.\n- SLO becomes a proper card with gradient surface, elevation, and an h-4 w-4\n  icon + text-sm font-semibold header, rows aligned to the card padding.\n\nVisual-only; no behavior, API, or data changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(dependency): clarify dependency impact chips are not live status\n\nThe Dependencies panel showed a red \"Critical\" / amber \"Degraded\" pill next to\neach neighbour, which - beside the live health dot and in the same status colours\n- read as though the dependency were down/degraded right now. It actually\ndescribes what the edge does to the system if the neighbour fails.\n\nThe impact chip now:\n- Drops the status (red/amber) palette entirely - impact is a static edge\n  attribute, so it uses a neutral chip ranked by emphasis; the health dot stays\n  the only colour-coded live signal on the row.\n- Uses impact-framed labels (\"Critical impact\", \"Degrading impact\",\n  \"Informational\") with an impact icon instead of a status dot.\n- Carries a direction-aware tooltip spelling out the exact consequence with both\n  system names (upstream and \"depended on by\" phrased from the right side).\n\nWording lives in a new pure presentDependencyImpact helper with unit tests.\nVisual-only; no behavior, API, or data changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* feat(backend-api): link Checkstack wordmark in email footers to checkstack.dev\n\nThe email notification footer (\"This is an automated notification from\nCheckstack.\") now renders \"Checkstack\" as a link to https://checkstack.dev via a\nnew renderFooterText helper. The footer string is HTML-escaped first and only a\ntrusted constant anchor is injected, so a custom footer cannot introduce markup;\na custom footer without the wordmark is left untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* feat(slo): count incident-forced downtime against SLO error budget\n\nWhen an incident forces a system unhealthy/degraded via its healthOverride,\nthat outage now opens an SLO downtime event (counted in the error budget and\nshown in recent downtime events) and closes when the incident is resolved,\ndeleted, or the override is cleared.\n\nThe override is applied read-time only, so the SLO engine (which subscribes to\nthe persisted health entity) never saw it. Add a targeted incident lifecycle\nhook (incident.lifecycle.changed, defined in incident-common, emitted from a\nsingle centralized helper used by both the router and the automation action\nhandlers) that slo-backend subscribes to via eventBus with work-queue delivery.\nReconcile opens/closes on effective health (checks OR active override): open one\nevent per objective when effectively down, close only when effectively healthy,\nso resolving an incident never closes a still-failing healthcheck outage and a\nchecks recovery never closes a still-active override.\n\n- New nullable `source` column (healthcheck|incident; NULL=healthcheck) on\n  slo_downtime_events distinguishes the cause and lets orphan-reconcile skip\n  incident-sourced events (their recovery isn''t in healthcheck history).\n- Serialize the open critical section with a per-objective advisory lock so the\n  health-down and incident consumers can''t double-open (RPCs kept outside the\n  lock transaction).\n- Wire the recovery-time resolver onto both engine instances so the daily job\n  closes recoverable orphans at true recovery time instead of deleting them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* feat(status-page): granular subscriptions and environment publishing\n\nTwo status-page enhancements sharing the same surfaces.\n\nGranular email subscriptions: instead of all-or-nothing, a public subscriber\nchooses categories (incidents / maintenance / health-status changes) and\nsystems (all on the page, or a subset). Defaults for new subscriptions: all\nsystems, incidents+maintenance (health off). Legacy subscribers (NULL scope)\nkeep receiving everything. The notify fan-out filters per subscriber by category\n(mapped from the audience event''s source plugin) and by system, intersected with\nthe systems the page currently surfaces; the subscribe endpoint keeps its\nconstant-time enumeration guard and silently clamps invalid input.\n\nEnvironment publishing: operators select which catalog environments a page\npublishes; a non-empty selection omits status, uptime, incidents and\nmaintenances for systems outside those environments. Environment ids are opaque\nto status-page-backend and threaded through WidgetResolveContext; the owning\ndomain widgets resolve env->systems via the catalog RPC (no platform->domain\nimport). Health widgets roll up only the selected environments and still fold in\nwhole-system incident overrides; the uptime widget gains a per-environment\nrun-stats filter and hides out-of-environment systems; incident/maintenance\nfeeds filter indirectly via each item''s affected systems.\n\nBackward compatible: new nullable columns (subscriber categories/system_ids,\nstatus page published_environment_ids); NULL/empty means \"all\". Incidents and\nmaintenances carry no environment, so a system in multiple environments makes\nits items visible on a page publishing any of them (documented).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* chore(ai-backend): regenerate docs index for SLO and status-page docs\n\nReflects the new documentation for incident-forced SLO downtime, granular\nstatus-page subscriptions, and status-page environment publishing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(ci): document markdown-remark override and update relocated-subscriptions e2e test\n\n- security/managed-overrides.json: document the @astrojs/markdown-remark\n  intentional dedup override (added for the mermaid docs-build fix) so\n  audit:overrides:check passes.\n- core/e2e/tests/notification.empty.spec.ts: subscriptions were moved off the\n  notification settings page onto /notification/subscriptions; update the stale\n  empty-state test to assert channels on the settings page and the subscription\n  manager + empty state on the dedicated page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(e2e): resolve status-page and rlac nav test regressions\n\n- StatusPageBuilderPage: rename the env-picker label \"Published environments\" ->\n  \"Visible environments\". The old label collided with the status-page e2e''s\n  `getByText(/Published/)` publish-confirmation matcher, so it matched the\n  always-present settings label instead of the real post-publish status and the\n  test raced to the public page before publish persisted.\n- rlac-team-scoped e2e: the batch added a public read-gated \"Incidents\" overview\n  nav (visible to everyone); assert on the manageCapability-gated \"Manage\n  Incidents\" nav instead, which is what an ungranted team member must not see.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"00e598c709ad9259b8cdd9e24a94d2b4303375b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/00e598c709ad9259b8cdd9e24a94d2b4303375b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/43e448440abbdca9e01eb95944f9312a7c108d62","verification":{"payload":"tree 00e598c709ad9259b8cdd9e24a94d2b4303375b1\nparent 2a1016c5029a8c304a6c5d03655bfc5b254fff4d\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783576553 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783576553 +0200\n\nBeta feedback, performance, and status-page/SLO features (#420)\n\n* feat: beta feedback fixes, N+1/perf optimizations, and query profiler\n\nA large checkpoint batch spanning user-feedback fixes (from @stuajnht''s\nbeta feedback), performance/N+1 work, observability, and a docs build fix.\n39 changesets; see each for scope. Highlights:\n\nUser feedback (features & bugfixes)\n- Health checks: SNMP strategy/collector; environment templating extended\n  across every built-in check type (+ SNMP host/OID, script cwd; script\n  bodies intentionally not templatable); fix HTTP 400 when opening Anomaly\n  Defaults on an unsaved check; clarified \"connect a satellite\" assignment\n  docs.\n- Status pages: custom-domain pages load (skip cross-origin /api/config\n  probe; CORS admits verified domains); group widgets collapse-when-healthy;\n  incident/maintenance deep links + minimal custom-domain router; anonymous\n  email subscriptions (double opt-in) + admin list/remove; group-scoped\n  incident/maintenance widgets; announcements widget.\n- Incidents/maintenance: Markdown; edit/delete updates + published-time edit\n  + manager-only edit history; three-way update visibility\n  (public/logged_in/internal); \"Keep Current (status)\"; internal notes;\n  logged-out overview pages + nav; fix grey `minor`/`monitoring` status\n  colours (app + status page); editable hotlinks (incident/maintenance/\n  catalog system links).\n- Notifications: latest update text in the body (incident + maintenance);\n  name the failing health check; generic outgoing webhook channel (with\n  SSRF/egress guard); \"Your Subscriptions\" moved to its own page.\n- Misc: API-docs examples use BASE_URL from the OpenAPI server; edit\n  satellite name/region without touching the token; catalog group sort\n  order; SLO error budget can exclude scheduled maintenance windows.\n\nPerformance / N+1\n- Catalog browse: bulk-data boundary slot removes per-row health/incident/\n  maintenance/SLO/dependency/subscription N+1s.\n- Status-page widgets: bulk-by-id resolvers (getBulkRunStats, bulk update\n  fetches) replace per-item RPC fan-out.\n- Backends: batched anomaly/notification/automation reads; scoped-db\n  transaction batching across catalog/slo/automation/dependency and remaining\n  backends; maintenance cron transition batched; secrets resolve active\n  backend once per batch.\n- Frontend: coalesce realtime signal invalidations to stop health-status\n  refetch storms.\n\nObservability\n- DB query/transaction duration histograms + pg_stat_statements export\n  (opt-in via CHECKSTACK_METRICS_ENABLED); profiling analyzer script under\n  core/scripts.\n\nBuild/tooling\n- Fix docs build warning by deduping @astrojs/markdown-remark to ^7.2.0\n  (astro-mermaid resolved a stale copy lacking isUnifiedProcessor).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(healthcheck-script): transport-only success/error aggregate tiles\n\nThe Script strategy''s mergeResult read the pre-collector per-run shape\n(metadata.success/executionTimeMs/timedOut), which is undefined in the\ncollector-based model, so Success Rate and Avg Execution Time tiles read\n0% / 0ms while per-run charts were correct. It then briefly used run.status,\nwhich conflates assertion failures with genuine errors.\n\nDerive the aggregates from the run''s transport signals stored under\nmetadata.collectors[<id>] (_collectorError, timedOut) plus a top-level error,\nmatching every other strategy and .claude/rules/healthcheck-collectors.md:\nSuccess Rate and Errors reflect only whether the probe completed, independent\nof assertion outcomes. avgExecutionTime uses run.latencyMs. Assertion failures\n(_assertionFailed) no longer lower Success Rate or count as Errors; they remain\nvisible as unhealthy in the health timeline.\n\nAdds real-shape regression tests: assertion-failure-is-not-an-error, genuine\ntransport error counts, and timeout counts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(catalog): consistent card design for incidents and SLO overview panels\n\nThe \"active incidents\" and \"SLO\" panels on the system overview rendered as thin\nrounded-md banner strips, inconsistent with the maintenance, dependencies,\nhealth-checks and anomaly cards. Restyle both to the shared card recipe\n(rounded-[var(--d-card-r)], from-surface-2/to-surface gradient, p-[var(--d-pad)],\nshared panel shadow).\n\n- Incidents match the sibling maintenance banner: status-colored left accent,\n  large count + caption, severity pills preserved; loading/empty states updated.\n- SLO becomes a proper card with gradient surface, elevation, and an h-4 w-4\n  icon + text-sm font-semibold header, rows aligned to the card padding.\n\nVisual-only; no behavior, API, or data changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(dependency): clarify dependency impact chips are not live status\n\nThe Dependencies panel showed a red \"Critical\" / amber \"Degraded\" pill next to\neach neighbour, which - beside the live health dot and in the same status colours\n- read as though the dependency were down/degraded right now. It actually\ndescribes what the edge does to the system if the neighbour fails.\n\nThe impact chip now:\n- Drops the status (red/amber) palette entirely - impact is a static edge\n  attribute, so it uses a neutral chip ranked by emphasis; the health dot stays\n  the only colour-coded live signal on the row.\n- Uses impact-framed labels (\"Critical impact\", \"Degrading impact\",\n  \"Informational\") with an impact icon instead of a status dot.\n- Carries a direction-aware tooltip spelling out the exact consequence with both\n  system names (upstream and \"depended on by\" phrased from the right side).\n\nWording lives in a new pure presentDependencyImpact helper with unit tests.\nVisual-only; no behavior, API, or data changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* feat(backend-api): link Checkstack wordmark in email footers to checkstack.dev\n\nThe email notification footer (\"This is an automated notification from\nCheckstack.\") now renders \"Checkstack\" as a link to https://checkstack.dev via a\nnew renderFooterText helper. The footer string is HTML-escaped first and only a\ntrusted constant anchor is injected, so a custom footer cannot introduce markup;\na custom footer without the wordmark is left untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* feat(slo): count incident-forced downtime against SLO error budget\n\nWhen an incident forces a system unhealthy/degraded via its healthOverride,\nthat outage now opens an SLO downtime event (counted in the error budget and\nshown in recent downtime events) and closes when the incident is resolved,\ndeleted, or the override is cleared.\n\nThe override is applied read-time only, so the SLO engine (which subscribes to\nthe persisted health entity) never saw it. Add a targeted incident lifecycle\nhook (incident.lifecycle.changed, defined in incident-common, emitted from a\nsingle centralized helper used by both the router and the automation action\nhandlers) that slo-backend subscribes to via eventBus with work-queue delivery.\nReconcile opens/closes on effective health (checks OR active override): open one\nevent per objective when effectively down, close only when effectively healthy,\nso resolving an incident never closes a still-failing healthcheck outage and a\nchecks recovery never closes a still-active override.\n\n- New nullable `source` column (healthcheck|incident; NULL=healthcheck) on\n  slo_downtime_events distinguishes the cause and lets orphan-reconcile skip\n  incident-sourced events (their recovery isn''t in healthcheck history).\n- Serialize the open critical section with a per-objective advisory lock so the\n  health-down and incident consumers can''t double-open (RPCs kept outside the\n  lock transaction).\n- Wire the recovery-time resolver onto both engine instances so the daily job\n  closes recoverable orphans at true recovery time instead of deleting them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* feat(status-page): granular subscriptions and environment publishing\n\nTwo status-page enhancements sharing the same surfaces.\n\nGranular email subscriptions: instead of all-or-nothing, a public subscriber\nchooses categories (incidents / maintenance / health-status changes) and\nsystems (all on the page, or a subset). Defaults for new subscriptions: all\nsystems, incidents+maintenance (health off). Legacy subscribers (NULL scope)\nkeep receiving everything. The notify fan-out filters per subscriber by category\n(mapped from the audience event''s source plugin) and by system, intersected with\nthe systems the page currently surfaces; the subscribe endpoint keeps its\nconstant-time enumeration guard and silently clamps invalid input.\n\nEnvironment publishing: operators select which catalog environments a page\npublishes; a non-empty selection omits status, uptime, incidents and\nmaintenances for systems outside those environments. Environment ids are opaque\nto status-page-backend and threaded through WidgetResolveContext; the owning\ndomain widgets resolve env->systems via the catalog RPC (no platform->domain\nimport). Health widgets roll up only the selected environments and still fold in\nwhole-system incident overrides; the uptime widget gains a per-environment\nrun-stats filter and hides out-of-environment systems; incident/maintenance\nfeeds filter indirectly via each item''s affected systems.\n\nBackward compatible: new nullable columns (subscriber categories/system_ids,\nstatus page published_environment_ids); NULL/empty means \"all\". Incidents and\nmaintenances carry no environment, so a system in multiple environments makes\nits items visible on a page publishing any of them (documented).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* chore(ai-backend): regenerate docs index for SLO and status-page docs\n\nReflects the new documentation for incident-forced SLO downtime, granular\nstatus-page subscriptions, and status-page environment publishing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(ci): document markdown-remark override and update relocated-subscriptions e2e test\n\n- security/managed-overrides.json: document the @astrojs/markdown-remark\n  intentional dedup override (added for the mermaid docs-build fix) so\n  audit:overrides:check passes.\n- core/e2e/tests/notification.empty.spec.ts: subscriptions were moved off the\n  notification settings page onto /notification/subscriptions; update the stale\n  empty-state test to assert channels on the settings page and the subscription\n  manager + empty state on the dedicated page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n* fix(e2e): resolve status-page and rlac nav test regressions\n\n- StatusPageBuilderPage: rename the env-picker label \"Published environments\" ->\n  \"Visible environments\". The old label collided with the status-page e2e''s\n  `getByText(/Published/)` publish-confirmation matcher, so it matched the\n  always-present settings label instead of the real post-publish status and the\n  test raced to the public page before publish persisted.\n- rlac-team-scoped e2e: the batch added a public read-gated \"Incidents\" overview\n  nav (visible to everyone); assert on the manageCapability-gated \"Manage\n  Incidents\" nav instead, which is what an ungranted team member must not see.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8p5PjRH1VS7iLXECyHos5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTzfpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgpYQACbM+BMWBhY78hp81c+VjaQw\nGWDv3xK6rRV1Id9zO/691G3ARK5M4tx1Od4DF1NLha2/m7VaIq4d8nm8tYzAeQn9\nxMsdHU/18aNU7ZDbjCOWyquRmtJEJsGSuVqVK8EgxvkNvkGrsU/1K2TZU2OAFFOP\ns0oIQ2xPkT7VT2fo+3ImKEQnjOZKB5jUwdiTrvo3nSf1Mhd9bQ7Zg8jxXmGYh0+Y\nKCqcHCfWDrq3rob+QlHrwdDEjowGf10q1pT5osIyfww3Jgv3Z60e49JceZcYljQg\n0QBrKcknk0FfJlsKDLpnZhXhylEA6TjwicUJ3toMqmesRLCAt482Pa9kLMnQY1lL\nQE9rfYJAoOnmYmzFZ6w4QdUuFa9/N3sMGMCatIqjTuXEQ8cWMpZAyXxnMT24/rgV\nuefnEeoZUnrZbqomoXQjcZfjd1ZdPqdJtYwdbp8AeVUsG/bcdOnvFQPHenAvqD6E\nDvInHXW9n8SiWL9EsIJyqBdgToLdeVUbZaMieii5H2jQKcqUqv2bY5ezrxuiB0Cv\n0tXnsBDebHFnj8oTDw/dCgYXURcdv+oEXCot3aE/sohuhh06vbCxd0cZi1RThZP