"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/fc64fad46a1ad80d03e1c6601bc474f06570e16b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T14:15:44Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T14:15:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dependency): scope-matrix, dependency-aware map layout, system panel (#413)\n\nScope dependencies to a (check, environment) matrix with per-cell severity,\ngive the dependency map a dependency-aware automatic layout, and add a\nread-only up/downstream dependency panel to system detail pages.\n\nScope matrix:\n- A dependency can now watch specific (check?, env?) slices of the upstream,\n  each with its own severity, instead of only the whole-system rollup. With no\n  cells configured the default (any check, any env) is unchanged.\n- Per-environment slices are evaluated on their own, so a scoped dependency\n  catches an env-specific outage the worst-wins rollup would hide. Backed by a\n  new `getBulkSystemHealthMatrix` healthcheck contract.\n- Forward-only migration adds a nullable `environment_id` and makes\n  `health_check_id` nullable on the scope-cell store.\n\nMap layout:\n- Replace the square grid with a layered (Sugiyama) layout: upstream to the\n  right, longest-path layering, barycenter crossing-reduction ordering, and\n  edgeless systems parked to the side. Saved positions are never moved; new\n  systems drop into a tidy block in the free space below.\n- Add \"Center on box\" (rebuild around a selected system) and \"Reset layout\"\n  (re-arrange every box) toolbar controls.\n\nSystem panel:\n- New read-only Dependencies panel on system detail pages listing upstream and\n  downstream neighbours with a live health dot and impact severity, gated to\n  global dependency-map readers OR team managers of the system.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d7a884d562ff57a387537e8dfa3242e49790a681","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/d7a884d562ff57a387537e8dfa3242e49790a681"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/fc64fad46a1ad80d03e1c6601bc474f06570e16b","verification":{"payload":"tree d7a884d562ff57a387537e8dfa3242e49790a681\nparent 390d9cf349b8178375725bee0ac54c4de0bcff83\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783347344 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783347344 +0200\n\nfeat(dependency): scope-matrix, dependency-aware map layout, system panel (#413)\n\nScope dependencies to a (check, environment) matrix with per-cell severity,\ngive the dependency map a dependency-aware automatic layout, and add a\nread-only up/downstream dependency panel to system detail pages.\n\nScope matrix:\n- A dependency can now watch specific (check?, env?) slices of the upstream,\n  each with its own severity, instead of only the whole-system rollup. With no\n  cells configured the default (any check, any env) is unchanged.\n- Per-environment slices are evaluated on their own, so a scoped dependency\n  catches an env-specific outage the worst-wins rollup would hide. Backed by a\n  new `getBulkSystemHealthMatrix` healthcheck contract.\n- Forward-only migration adds a nullable `environment_id` and makes\n  `health_check_id` nullable on the scope-cell store.\n\nMap layout:\n- Replace the square grid with a layered (Sugiyama) layout: upstream to the\n  right, longest-path layering, barycenter crossing-reduction ordering, and\n  edgeless systems parked to the side. Saved positions are never moved; new\n  systems drop into a tidy block in the free space below.\n- Add \"Center on box\" (rebuild around a selected system) and \"Reset layout\"\n  (re-arrange every box) toolbar controls.\n\nSystem panel:\n- New read-only Dependencies panel on system detail pages listing upstream and\n  downstream neighbours with a live health dot and impact severity, gated to\n  global dependency-map readers OR team managers of the system.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS7iQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcoYQABrHSWauBQ1todPa13qlnAlk\nF7oqRHI+oqDRJrnVGKcrPlBe/WLAb68G44BhjTkodc8tpDd8UhoH4A4AOJpPYwN/\nPdYoNCagkuja8xyK6CtXO3M6Qc1I3r8L+xRx5Xe4qtijnXv3YPQY74gmqRf+GbGb\nfnyp5z1A435/VXuowllcc7mUd7PRWJ3/VF1kfvR9vAzDvsPzlrsYyEi1Uze/e1e9\nyt4NDr46xI7zeB0KoyRdJS1zkHZ6Hzk0vmmzUdv1U84q0JxCKieubW1cx7VZ1wJS\nTssCuCu46S0qImbPrHK5oFGaAdeKBOoXHkecG9po2wYhCcSpYxxRWzIYyaUy3qnf\nzpO5lJLhoJMCDICJ6oxKoSt7Z96q5dVUzh7QitLdmW2MBFsjIUofLsIOKqCDT5pA\nXzl2d0HeeFnnILO1Uyqh04o9aefXpZMDA1PR25D9ecT0fhVPhC97bBKPxOfff9W6\n643lKI/6LPjv+qdgpMvszQJ0fgwFJtNgufFK8tf6z7yaCJqMZh5r9Dd1M+uO0PiG\nNGFG+QwhPFHigdrslOZGQSbhkUPyIm7c6s21XW/VdKXyAxE1LEcrJ0gOvI2uRJAy\nM+gjiGN7ev2J0T+oHFNHMlZkxp6AUplSKzhJap2f1wEXSRq7TcBZ2mla6yDBXSZH\nX3X5Lu4b9zTXqw+jv8dl\n=Eeo6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T14:15:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/fc64fad46a1ad80d03e1c6601bc474f06570e16b","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKGZjNjRmYWQ0NmExYWQ4MGQwM2UxYzY2MDFiYzQ3NGYwNjU3MGUxNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/390d9cf349b8178375725bee0ac54c4de0bcff83","sha":"390d9cf349b8178375725bee0ac54c4de0bcff83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/390d9cf349b8178375725bee0ac54c4de0bcff83"}],"sha":"fc64fad46a1ad80d03e1c6601bc474f06570e16b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/fc64fad46a1ad80d03e1c6601bc474f06570e16b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/390d9cf349b8178375725bee0ac54c4de0bcff83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T08:17:39Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T08:17:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(healthcheck-container): monitor Docker/Podman containers via read-only socket-proxy (#412)\n\n* feat(healthcheck-container): monitor Docker/Podman containers via read-only socket-proxy\n\nAdd a Container health-check strategy for containers that expose no external\nservice. It reports container existence, running state, healthcheck status,\nexit code, restart count and OOM-killed (Container Status collector) and\nCPU/memory usage (Container Stats collector), all as assertable metrics.\n\nCheckstack never touches the raw container socket: the strategy speaks the\nDocker Engine / Podman libpod REST API over a unix socket path OR an http(s)\nendpoint, so operators point it at a read-only socket-proxy (POST=0) or a\nrootless Podman socket. Only GET endpoints are used. A stopped or missing\ncontainer is a successful collection whose metrics feed assertions (per the\ntransport-failure-vs-metric rule); only an unreachable endpoint fails the check.\nRuns locally on core (includeLocal) or on a pinned satellite.\n\nThe hardened proxy compose is maintained in one canonical file\n(deploy/socket-proxy/docker-compose.yml) that operators `include:`; the docs and\nin-product setup guide reference it instead of duplicating YAML.\n\nAdds an optional `setupInstructions` (Markdown) field to the strategy contract,\nrendered as a collapsible \"Setup guide\" in the editor, and removes a stale\nhand-written HealthCheckStrategyDto interface that shadowed the Zod-inferred DTO.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n* test(healthcheck-container): CI-safe end-to-end transport integration test\n\nDrive the real strategy + collectors over a real HTTP endpoint and a real unix\nsocket against an in-process Bun.serve stand-in for the Docker Engine API. This\ncovers the actual transport path (endpoint resolution, HTTP, unix socket, JSON\nparsing, collector execution) that the mocked-fetch unit tests bypass, including\nthe transport-failure boundary (real 404 -> exists:false without throwing; a\nconnection-refused endpoint throws). No Docker daemon needed, so it runs in the\nfast test lane in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n* test(healthcheck-container): real socket-proxy constellation integration test\n\nAdd container-proxy.it.test.ts: stands up the actual documented deployment - the\nreal lscr.io/linuxserver/socket-proxy in front of the host Docker socket\n(CONTAINERS=1 INFO=1 POST=0, socket mounted :ro) - and drives the real strategy\nand collectors through it. Asserts both halves of the security posture the\nBun.serve test cannot: reads (status + stats) work through the proxy, and the\nread-only POST=0 proxy returns 403 on a kill (the container stays running), so a\ncompromised instance cannot control the host. Also verifies a missing container\nreads as exists:false through the proxy.\n\nGated on CHECKSTACK_IT AND a live Docker daemon, so it runs in the existing\n`integration` CI job (ubuntu-latest has Docker) and skips cleanly where Docker\nis absent. Documented in the integration-lane guide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"542256cf6355370a986b21c3abb65cca763433db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/542256cf6355370a986b21c3abb65cca763433db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/390d9cf349b8178375725bee0ac54c4de0bcff83","verification":{"payload":"tree 542256cf6355370a986b21c3abb65cca763433db\nparent 9d30324c30ecb47deebb8890f4f7a781e9e6fa3f\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783325859 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783325859 +0200\n\nfeat(healthcheck-container): monitor Docker/Podman containers via read-only socket-proxy (#412)\n\n* feat(healthcheck-container): monitor Docker/Podman containers via read-only socket-proxy\n\nAdd a Container health-check strategy for containers that expose no external\nservice. It reports container existence, running state, healthcheck status,\nexit code, restart count and OOM-killed (Container Status collector) and\nCPU/memory usage (Container Stats collector), all as assertable metrics.\n\nCheckstack never touches the raw container socket: the strategy speaks the\nDocker Engine / Podman libpod REST API over a unix socket path OR an http(s)\nendpoint, so operators point it at a read-only socket-proxy (POST=0) or a\nrootless Podman socket. Only GET endpoints are used. A stopped or missing\ncontainer is a successful collection whose metrics feed assertions (per the\ntransport-failure-vs-metric rule); only an unreachable endpoint fails the check.\nRuns locally on core (includeLocal) or on a pinned satellite.\n\nThe hardened proxy compose is maintained in one canonical file\n(deploy/socket-proxy/docker-compose.yml) that operators `include:`; the docs and\nin-product setup guide reference it instead of duplicating YAML.\n\nAdds an optional `setupInstructions` (Markdown) field to the strategy contract,\nrendered as a collapsible \"Setup guide\" in the editor, and removes a stale\nhand-written HealthCheckStrategyDto interface that shadowed the Zod-inferred DTO.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n* test(healthcheck-container): CI-safe end-to-end transport integration test\n\nDrive the real strategy + collectors over a real HTTP endpoint and a real unix\nsocket against an in-process Bun.serve stand-in for the Docker Engine API. This\ncovers the actual transport path (endpoint resolution, HTTP, unix socket, JSON\nparsing, collector execution) that the mocked-fetch unit tests bypass, including\nthe transport-failure boundary (real 404 -> exists:false without throwing; a\nconnection-refused endpoint throws). No Docker daemon needed, so it runs in the\nfast test lane in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n* test(healthcheck-container): real socket-proxy constellation integration test\n\nAdd container-proxy.it.test.ts: stands up the actual documented deployment - the\nreal lscr.io/linuxserver/socket-proxy in front of the host Docker socket\n(CONTAINERS=1 INFO=1 POST=0, socket mounted :ro) - and drives the real strategy\nand collectors through it. Asserts both halves of the security posture the\nBun.serve test cannot: reads (status + stats) work through the proxy, and the\nread-only POST=0 proxy returns 403 on a kill (the container stays running), so a\ncompromised instance cannot control the host. Also verifies a missing container\nreads as exists:false through the proxy.\n\nGated on CHECKSTACK_IT AND a live Docker daemon, so it runs in the existing\n`integration` CI job (ubuntu-latest has Docker) and skips cleanly where Docker\nis absent. Documented in the integration-lane guide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS2SjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUyAQABu159olZvfEHJss5o27WP3y\nNs9SuPpePkCqqJasPse7vxw+o84dtLzliSyHzXGp3FgqX9tTAwI4RbnetsVeB8kt\nEzjBtN0v3Z9FYwQ15wzCmkr/tJEEumRhBOrflz0WyD9dUHR83Xd4+n3oRJHZslCq\nbpm3FPvQ7cjVjhysa0s4xxm+9SKsqlZj/Z8V3838Dhv8CaZ/ihdiqzmuwHQRr7kx\nGfYhYMEa88KgLs9xaZOTq+UEKWBx+Lrw85n5WDPsgus1jWFCsTFX8vpT9Yx2gqUq\nxKOHOEmO4bk3vPJNP8xJR7zmrPlFW5AEUiFkBaaNbvNHNaNXAaOYrHC7CncY73UH\n6V+wFg5bnF0rh1hL8ukB/RS6xQuNEc3oQbPfB5ROE2yqTXa3+RDj4dGtBQDzsBwR\nN8Hhb8uHOk5Q/apuj8sc18xQL1cOb1ifAVCsog6eQwsAFcWKNU6TWsiBbSqXkDYq\nDQ8mfwEME5iTdM1HHaUB7sBLbuubK5gwCP/7oEIkB8G3opd6qx4rM8E75SjTfzxd\ngOx2uovf0A57n5aC9UxWryFmudm3oNlHlYl2OsrIsGKuHhPpdAwHuqvTOb2S3iF/\nYiUzJFbHfw/pVUgDXXi65Re5xApOXAfU+ElHelpkBJddlK84q07iYJ2x++aq1ttV\nMvFJ19ZhndW7sX1O2Cqs\n=jTtZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T08:17:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/390d9cf349b8178375725bee0ac54c4de0bcff83","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKDM5MGQ5Y2YzNDliODE3ODM3NTcyNWJlZTBhYzU0YzRkZTBiY2ZmODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/9d30324c30ecb47deebb8890f4f7a781e9e6fa3f","sha":"9d30324c30ecb47deebb8890f4f7a781e9e6fa3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/9d30324c30ecb47deebb8890f4f7a781e9e6fa3f"}],"sha":"390d9cf349b8178375725bee0ac54c4de0bcff83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/390d9cf349b8178375725bee0ac54c4de0bcff83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/9d30324c30ecb47deebb8890f4f7a781e9e6fa3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T22:18:19Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T22:18:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(incident): optional incident-driven system health override (#411)\n\nIncidents can optionally force the health status of their affected\nsystems while active. A new \"Override system health\" choice (Degraded or\nUnhealthy) on the incident editor is folded into each affected system''s\nderived health via worst-wins, so it shows on every health surface\n(status pages, dashboards, dependency map, catalog badge) and lifts\nautomatically when the incident resolves. A health check reporting a\nworse status still wins; forcing healthy is not offered. This covers\ncomponents no automated check can monitor.\n\nThe override is a deliberate operator choice, independent of the\nincident''s severity. Wiring:\n\n- incident-common/backend: nullable `health_override` column + enum\n  (forward-only migration), persisted on create/update, and a new\n  service-typed `getActiveHealthOverrides` RPC returning active overrides\n  per system.\n- healthcheck: the fold is applied in the two user-facing RPC handlers\n  (single + bulk), OUTSIDE the status cache (always live) and NEVER in\n  the shared getSystemHealthStatus deriver, so SLO downtime, the AI\n  signals scan, and the persisted health entity stay checks-only (no\n  double-count, no incident->health->automation loop). The read is\n  best-effort: if the incident RPC fails, checks-only status is returned.\n- healthcheck-common: system-health response gains an optional `override`\n  field naming the contributing incident; the health badge shows it on\n  hover.\n\nDocs: Incidents and Health checks concept pages document the override and\nthe worst-wins fold; docs index regenerated.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebbd3910e077eccd566abc0fb7250e2ffee1950f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/ebbd3910e077eccd566abc0fb7250e2ffee1950f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/9d30324c30ecb47deebb8890f4f7a781e9e6fa3f","verification":{"payload":"tree ebbd3910e077eccd566abc0fb7250e2ffee1950f\nparent 0b272dca1aa8aa11e80d1cf1714268bcd1da5bd2\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783289899 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783289899 +0200\n\nfeat(incident): optional incident-driven system health override (#411)\n\nIncidents can optionally force the health status of their affected\nsystems while active. A new \"Override system health\" choice (Degraded or\nUnhealthy) on the incident editor is folded into each affected system''s\nderived health via worst-wins, so it shows on every health surface\n(status pages, dashboards, dependency map, catalog badge) and lifts\nautomatically when the incident resolves. A health check reporting a\nworse status still wins; forcing healthy is not offered. This covers\ncomponents no automated check can monitor.\n\nThe override is a deliberate operator choice, independent of the\nincident''s severity. Wiring:\n\n- incident-common/backend: nullable `health_override` column + enum\n  (forward-only migration), persisted on create/update, and a new\n  service-typed `getActiveHealthOverrides` RPC returning active overrides\n  per system.\n- healthcheck: the fold is applied in the two user-facing RPC handlers\n  (single + bulk), OUTSIDE the status cache (always live) and NEVER in\n  the shared getSystemHealthStatus deriver, so SLO downtime, the AI\n  signals scan, and the persisted health entity stay checks-only (no\n  double-count, no incident->health->automation loop). The read is\n  best-effort: if the incident RPC fails, checks-only status is returned.\n- healthcheck-common: system-health response gains an optional `override`\n  field naming the contributing incident; the health badge shows it on\n  hover.\n\nDocs: Incidents and Health checks concept pages document the override and\nthe worst-wins fold; docs index regenerated.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>