lZWJiODg5MGY0ZjdhNzgxZTllNmZhM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/0b272dca1aa8aa11e80d1cf1714268bcd1da5bd2","sha":"0b272dca1aa8aa11e80d1cf1714268bcd1da5bd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/0b272dca1aa8aa11e80d1cf1714268bcd1da5bd2"}],"sha":"9d30324c30ecb47deebb8890f4f7a781e9e6fa3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/9d30324c30ecb47deebb8890f4f7a781e9e6fa3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/0b272dca1aa8aa11e80d1cf1714268bcd1da5bd2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T21:15:21Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T21:15:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(docs): restore light-mode theme on the docs site (#410)\n\nThe Starlight custom stylesheet is injected unlayered via `customCss`, so\nits token overrides beat Starlight''s own `@layer starlight.base` rules\nregardless of specificity. The file defined the gray ramp, `--sl-color-white`\nand `--sl-color-black` in a single unqualified `:root`, so those dark values\nalso applied in light mode and clobbered Starlight''s `:root[data-theme=''light'']`\npalette. The result: light mode kept a dark page background\n(`--sl-color-bg: var(--sl-color-black)`) and dark surfaces, making code, links\nand environment-variable text hard to read.\n\nSplit the ramp per theme, mirroring Starlight''s dark-first structure: the base\n`:root` now carries the dark palette (identical values to the previous\n`[data-theme=\"dark\"]` block, so dark mode is unchanged) and a new\n`:root[data-theme=\"light\"]` block supplies the inverted light palette. Because\nthis block is also unlayered, it wins in light mode and the background and\nsurfaces render light again.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f864e8cdbdba5cb2e2bcc5a8966bb260d26cdac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/6f864e8cdbdba5cb2e2bcc5a8966bb260d26cdac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/0b272dca1aa8aa11e80d1cf1714268bcd1da5bd2","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f864e8cdbdba5cb2e2bcc5a8966bb260d26cdac\nparent b218e3ef2512ac0e18bb5fb8d78556d72ab8f435\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783286121 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783286121 +0200\n\nfix(docs): restore light-mode theme on the docs site (#410)\n\nThe Starlight custom stylesheet is injected unlayered via `customCss`, so\nits token overrides beat Starlight''s own `@layer starlight.base` rules\nregardless of specificity. The file defined the gray ramp, `--sl-color-white`\nand `--sl-color-black` in a single unqualified `:root`, so those dark values\nalso applied in light mode and clobbered Starlight''s `:root[data-theme=''light'']`\npalette. The result: light mode kept a dark page background\n(`--sl-color-bg: var(--sl-color-black)`) and dark surfaces, making code, links\nand environment-variable text hard to read.\n\nSplit the ramp per theme, mirroring Starlight''s dark-first structure: the base\n`:root` now carries the dark palette (identical values to the previous\n`[data-theme=\"dark\"]` block, so dark mode is unchanged) and a new\n`:root[data-theme=\"light\"]` block supplies the inverted light palette. Because\nthis block is also unlayered, it wins in light mode and the background and\nsurfaces render light again.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSslpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFFIQAGoameZKSJgfbszhvh4LzKtJ\no1YrCxKk9mJiBfqDzPX6imMBv6dT3BBf8keQu4qutHkHb3YLSTsljvBuhTNTsj02\nq6TjpcbZ8YVdvCRi8i+pIvdgrcO9J8qXzu9kxIrXw7z7u7ItcXoB71SUnqnT/kF+\ncyhYOO0pNTg2s7LqHmqP33IPeu1mQCnF/7ODLlHK67ERldJMLRfXQ8S69n9R9TLD\nymL0PFXeNpFQTLy8SqnKxYn2NOtzT9tKDhx8KmMrAU8mmybwD4W0RkpNWnqV+STj\nXlllvTW7R4dY6dy0gzxiJ/0hqvw/jCjnUF7FZVdXaYHTT6EO4k7cjSiJg/hg97pf\nkh3NzdDmlwg1i2XEAmokPwPKgQK1uqUtoIWB3qLxfF+R3Kv7RuCnFtP5U/71KvFd\npm592TIP6WIxc1/DgrQc9G4YzNl28HAP0gLP1js0sCpBXykk13dTK/7v58GoD7oo\nfm22QuxLigNs3n99kBJA4rumvaey1Oa1KlaGCyF8fQyjtuYH9LUBZZohdn5gAQGy\na2Tw/6XWO/i2kxRSPhfsdh+6rnvJ2vMnRloKr2Hp57JJzmN4p0A9Tm3+KCt9sfjZ\n0xHscg0eKiXByWfwLO8rk5fZ9buB93UBk2ZsbRlwtbstSmLH63w6vKWmrOEsBHlB\n13Cj4iAkV0jubxtQd42P\n=d2z3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-05T21:15:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/0b272dca1aa8aa11e80d1cf1714268bcd1da5bd2","node_id":"C_kwDOQrp5TdoAKDBiMjcyZGNhMWFhOGFhMTFlODBkMWNmMTcxNDI2OGJjZDFkYTViZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer/checkstack/commit/b218e3ef2512ac0e18bb5fb8d78556d72ab8f435","sha":"b218e3ef2512ac0e18bb5fb8d78556d72ab8f435","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/b218e3ef2512ac0e18bb5fb8d78556d72ab8f435"}],"sha":"0b272dca1aa8aa11e80d1cf1714268bcd1da5bd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/0b272dca1aa8aa11e80d1cf1714268bcd1da5bd2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27201677?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/enyineer","id":27201677,"login":"enyineer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjAxNjc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enyineer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/commits/b218e3ef2512ac0e18bb5fb8d78556d72ab8f435/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T21:08:15Z","email":"nico.enking@gmail.com","name":"Nico"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T21:08:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui): shared sortable/searchable DataTable + consistent row actions (#408)\n\n* feat(ui): shared sortable/searchable DataTable + consistent row actions\n\nAdd a shared DataTable to @checkstack/ui (TanStack Table under a typed house\nAPI): click-to-sort headers, a global search box, an opaque bg-card surface\n(fixes previously transparent, hard-to-read tables), a renderMobileCard branch,\nand getRowProps ARIA/keyboard passthrough for interactive rows. Add RowActions/\nRowAction as the one canonical row-action style (subtle ghost icon button;\ndestructive=red tint, success=green tint, never a loud filled button).\n\nMigrate every list table (~29 sites across catalog, healthcheck, auth, incident,\nmaintenance, slo, gitops, about, api-docs, pluginmanager, satellite, cache,\nqueue, notification, automation, announcement, integration) to DataTable and\nroute all row actions through RowActions, preserving access gating, bulk\nselection, extension slots, provenance locks, and mobile layouts. Severity and\nstatus sort by impact rank. Remove section headings that echoed the page title\non single-table pages. Remove the now-dead ResponsiveTable/MobileCardList and\nEmptyRunsTableRow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n* test(e2e): fix DataTable-migration selector drift\n\nScope Infrastructure Settings tab-rail clicks to the new\n`Infrastructure settings` nav so they no longer collide with the\nsame-named sortable column-header buttons the DataTable migration adds\n(Queue/Cache). Match the health-check empty state by text now that it\nrenders in a Card, and drop the removed \"Satellite Nodes\" heading\nassertion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n* test(e2e): update automation/incident row affordances for DataTable\n\nThe automation list \"Runs\" link is now a `RowAction` button (\"View\nruns\"), and the system incident-history rows navigate via `onRowClick`\ninstead of a per-row `<Link>`. Update both specs to target the button\nand the row so they no longer time out clicking a removed link.\n\nVerified locally: `bun run test:e2e incident.spec.ts automation.spec.ts`\n-> 59 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cac67a1f3bef47b20b0b6b63c39f3e1aacfbdbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/trees/9cac67a1f3bef47b20b0b6b63c39f3e1aacfbdbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enyineer/checkstack/git/commits/b218e3ef2512ac0e18bb5fb8d78556d72ab8f435","verification":{"payload":"tree 9cac67a1f3bef47b20b0b6b63c39f3e1aacfbdbf\nparent 565920896e369a4beefa1c5c600bfddcd3d84847\nauthor Nico <nico.enking@gmail.com> 1783285695 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783285695 +0200\n\nfeat(ui): shared sortable/searchable DataTable + consistent row actions (#408)\n\n* feat(ui): shared sortable/searchable DataTable + consistent row actions\n\nAdd a shared DataTable to @checkstack/ui (TanStack Table under a typed house\nAPI): click-to-sort headers, a global search box, an opaque bg-card surface\n(fixes previously transparent, hard-to-read tables), a renderMobileCard branch,\nand getRowProps ARIA/keyboard passthrough for interactive rows. Add RowActions/\nRowAction as the one canonical row-action style (subtle ghost icon button;\ndestructive=red tint, success=green tint, never a loud filled button).\n\nMigrate every list table (~29 sites across catalog, healthcheck, auth, incident,\nmaintenance, slo, gitops, about, api-docs, pluginmanager, satellite, cache,\nqueue, notification, automation, announcement, integration) to DataTable and\nroute all row actions through RowActions, preserving access gating, bulk\nselection, extension slots, provenance locks, and mobile layouts. Severity and\nstatus sort by impact rank. Remove section headings that echoed the page title\non single-table pages. Remove the now-dead ResponsiveTable/MobileCardList and\nEmptyRunsTableRow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n* test(e2e): fix DataTable-migration selector drift\n\nScope Infrastructure Settings tab-rail clicks to the new\n`Infrastructure settings` nav so they no longer collide with the\nsame-named sortable column-header buttons the DataTable migration adds\n(Queue/Cache). Match the health-check empty state by text now that it\nrenders in a Card, and drop the removed \"Satellite Nodes\" heading\nassertion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n* test(e2e): update automation/incident row affordances for DataTable\n\nThe automation list \"Runs\" link is now a `RowAction` button (\"View\nruns\"), and the system incident-history rows navigate via `onRowClick`\ninstead of a per-row `<Link>`. Update both specs to target the button\nand the row so they no longer time out clicking a removed link.\n\nVerified locally: `bun run test:e2e incident.spec.ts automation.spec.ts`\n-> 59 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014tB8vZmB9gDDpf285XoeLy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSse/CRC1aQ7uu