kotaB75","node_id":"U_kgDOCNaedQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakotaB75/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakotaB75/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakotaB75/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakotaB75/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakotaB75/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakotaB75","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakotaB75/meli-microfrontend-simulation/commits/4001029bf08e4f8f0a20c95c016da3c20f422f9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-21T01:16:24Z","email":"148282997+DakotaB75@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dakota Bazan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-21T01:16:24Z","email":"148282997+DakotaB75@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dakota Bazan"},"message":"Enterprise Microfrontend Simulation | React + TypeScript + Node.js BFF | CI/CD, Testing & Security\n\nThis repository demonstrates an enterprise-grade microfrontend architecture inspired by real practices at Mercado Libre.\n\nIt features two independently deployable React applications communicating via shared components and a global event bus, fully typed with TypeScript. The backend BFF (Node.js + Express) handles API orchestration and error management, while the architecture prioritizes performance, scalability, testability, and security.\n\nCI/CD pipelines, automated testing with Cypress & Playwright, CodeQL security scans, and secret validation scripts ensure production readiness. Branch strategy and modular design reflect real-world multi-team collaboration.\n\nThis project is a technical showcase of architectural decisions, tradeoffs, and senior-level engineering practices.","tree":{"sha":"132801f9aa737453d0c9342acb39d75c4d4f712d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakotaB75/meli-microfrontend-simulation/git/trees/132801f9aa737453d0c9342acb39d75c4d4f712d"},