ps://api.github.com/users/anwarika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anwarika/spark-engine/commit/535929825c06ef565c3585a111bd25740d90e9f8","node_id":"C_kwDOQsrd-toAKDUzNTkyOTgyNWMwNmVmNTY1YzM1ODVhMTExYmQyNTc0MGQ5MGU5Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anwarika/spark-engine/commit/9414ae7d9c991559c9e6cef6f5abe6fdbcd218ca","sha":"9414ae7d9c991559c9e6cef6f5abe6fdbcd218ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anwarika/spark-engine/commits/9414ae7d9c991559c9e6cef6f5abe6fdbcd218ca"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/anwarika/spark-engine/commit/28d4f5441741137e6080b11fd60069e65d8f3a14","sha":"28d4f5441741137e6080b11fd60069e65d8f3a14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anwarika/spark-engine/commits/28d4f5441741137e6080b11fd60069e65d8f3a14"}],"sha":"535929825c06ef565c3585a111bd25740d90e9f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anwarika/spark-engine/commits/535929825c06ef565c3585a111bd25740d90e9f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38044808?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anwarika","id":38044808,"login":"anwarika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MDQ0ODA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anwarika/spark-engine/commits/28d4f5441741137e6080b11fd60069e65d8f3a14/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-20T00:10:07Z","email":"38044808+anwarika@users.noreply.github.com","name":"anwarika"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-20T00:10:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: production-readiness overhaul — API keys, rate limiting, SDK po… (#10)\n\n…lish, playground, admin\n\nPhase 1a — API Key System\n- Add api_keys table (migration 20260419000000) with hash, scopes, RPM\nlimit, revoke support\n- POST/GET/DELETE /api/keys router with admin-scope guard\n- Auth middleware now reads sk_live_* keys from DB; backward-compat with\nlegacy Bearer/header auth\n- API key storage methods added to both PostgresStorage and\nSupabaseStorage\n\nPhase 2 — Rate Limiting + Scope-based Permissions\n- New RateLimitMiddleware: sliding-window Redis counter per key/tenant,\nRetry-After on 429\n- Graceful degradation when Redis is unavailable\n- require_scope() dependency factory wired onto /api/a2a/generate and\nkey routes\n\nPhase 3a+3b — Reliability Hardening\n- _llm_call_with_retry(): 45s timeout + exponential-backoff retry (max\n3) for LLM calls\n- /health expanded; new /ready readiness probe checks Postgres + Redis\nindependently\n- Audit log service (fire-and-forget) + audit_log table (migration\n20260419000001)\n\nPhase 1c — SDK Polish\n- New errors.ts: SparkAuthError, SparkPermissionError,\nSparkRateLimitError, SparkGenerationError, SparkTimeoutError\n- SparkClient: generateAndWait() one-liner, apiKey config field, key\nmanagement methods\n- SparkWidget: loading skeleton, error overlay with retry button,\nrenderSkeleton/renderError props\n\nPhase 1b+4a — Playground + Onboarding\n- Playground.tsx: live demo with 5 preset prompts, iframe preview, SDK\nsnippet copy\n- Playground is now the default landing tab\n\nPhase 3d — Data Bridge Expansion\n- POST /api/components/{id}/data/swap accepts ttl_seconds (60s–24h)\n- New PATCH /api/components/{id}/data: merge keys into existing data\nwithout full swap\n\nPhase 4b+4d — Admin Dashboard\n- GET /api/admin/stats: generation trend, pin count, key count, Redis\ncache hit rate\n- AdminDashboard.tsx: KPI cards + bar chart + period selector\n\nPhase 1d — Docs + Examples\n- docs/QUICKSTART.md: 5-step guide (start → key → generate → embed →\npin)\n- examples/nextjs-chat/: Next.js chat showing message → SparkWidget\npattern\n- examples/plain-js/index.html: zero-dependency embed with preset\nprompts\n\n## Description\n\n<!-- Describe your changes in detail -->\n\n## Motivation and Context\n\n<!-- Why is this change required? What problem does it solve? -->\n<!-- If it fixes an open issue, please link to the issue here. -->\n\nFixes #(issue)\n\n## Type of Change\n\n<!-- Put an `x` in all the boxes that apply -->\n\n- [ ] 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing\nfunctionality to change)\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Code refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test addition/update\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n<!-- Please describe the tests that you ran to verify your changes -->\n\n- [ ] Manual testing in development environment\n- [ ] Added/updated unit tests\n- [ ] Added/updated integration tests\n- [ ] Tested with multiple LLM providers\n- [ ] Tested data bridge functionality\n- [ ] Tested multi-tenant isolation\n\n## Checklist\n\n<!-- Put an `x` in all the boxes that apply -->\n\n- [ ] My code follows the code style of this project\n- [ ] I have updated the documentation accordingly\n- [ ] I have added tests to cover my changes\n- [ ] All new and existing tests passed\n- [ ] I have updated CHANGELOG.md\n- [ ] My changes generate no new linter warnings\n- [ ] I have checked my code for security issues\n\n## Screenshots (if applicable)\n\n<!-- Add screenshots to help explain your changes -->\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n<!-- Any additional information that reviewers should know -->","tree":{"sha":"e6ee568d1c2744b75de259f2f14830982fba271a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anwarika/spark-engine/git/trees/e6ee568d1c2744b75de259f2f14830982fba271a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anwarika/spark-engine/git/commits/28d4f5441741137e6080b11fd60069e65d8f3a14","verification":{"payload":"tree e6ee568d1c2744b75de259f2f14830982fba271a\nparent 37fdf3b2de1d9936d3efffa69da6c669eda4cc22\nparent 9414ae7d9c991559c9e6cef6f5abe6fdbcd218ca\nauthor anwarika <38044808+anwarika@users.noreply.github.com> 1776643807 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776643807 -0400\n\nfeat: production-readiness overhaul — API keys, rate limiting, SDK po… (#10)\n\n…lish, playground, admin\n\nPhase 1a — API Key System\n- Add api_keys table (migration 20260419000000) with hash, scopes, RPM\nlimit, revoke support\n- POST/GET/DELETE /api/keys router with admin-scope guard\n- Auth middleware now reads sk_live_* keys from DB; backward-compat with\nlegacy Bearer/header auth\n- API key storage methods added to both PostgresStorage and\nSupabaseStorage\n\nPhase 2 — Rate Limiting + Scope-based Permissions\n- New RateLimitMiddleware: sliding-window Redis counter per key/tenant,\nRetry-After on 429\n- Graceful degradation when Redis is unavailable\n- require_scope() dependency factory wired onto /api/a2a/generate and\nkey routes\n\nPhase 3a+3b — Reliability Hardening\n- _llm_call_with_retry(): 45s timeout + exponential-backoff retry (max\n3) for LLM calls\n- /health expanded; new /ready readiness probe checks Postgres + Redis\nindependently\n- Audit log service (fire-and-forget) + audit_log table (migration\n20260419000001)\n\nPhase 1c — SDK Polish\n- New errors.ts: SparkAuthError, SparkPermissionError,\nSparkRateLimitError, SparkGenerationError, SparkTimeoutError\n- SparkClient: generateAndWait() one-liner, apiKey config field, key\nmanagement methods\n- SparkWidget: loading skeleton, error overlay with retry button,\nrenderSkeleton/renderError props\n\nPhase 1b+4a — Playground + Onboarding\n- Playground.tsx: live demo with 5 preset prompts, iframe preview, SDK\nsnippet copy\n- Playground is now the default landing tab\n\nPhase 3d — Data Bridge Expansion\n- POST /api/components/{id}/data/swap accepts ttl_seconds (60s–24h)\n- New PATCH /api/components/{id}/data: merge keys into existing data\nwithout full swap\n\nPhase 4b+4d — Admin Dashboard\n- GET /api/admin/stats: generation trend, pin count, key count, Redis\ncache hit rate\n- AdminDashboard.tsx: KPI cards + bar chart + period selector\n\nPhase 1d — Docs + Examples\n- docs/QUICKSTART.md: 5-step guide (start → key → generate → embed →\npin)\n- examples/nextjs-chat/: Next.js chat showing message → SparkWidget\npattern\n- examples/plain-js/index.html: zero-dependency embed with preset\nprompts\n\n## Description\n\n<!-- Describe your changes in detail -->\n\n## Motivation and Context\n\n<!-- Why is this change required? What problem does it solve? -->\n<!-- If it fixes an open issue, please link to the issue here. -->\n\nFixes #(issue)\n\n## Type of Change\n\n<!-- Put an `x` in all the boxes that apply -->\n\n- [ ] 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing\nfunctionality to change)\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Code refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test addition/update\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n<!-- Please describe the tests that you ran to verify your changes -->\n\n- [ ] Manual testing in development environment\n- [ ] Added/updated unit tests\n- [ ] Added/updated integration tests\n- [ ] Tested with multiple LLM providers\n- [ ] Tested data bridge functionality\n- [ ] Tested multi-tenant isolation\n\n## Checklist\n\n<!-- Put an `x` in all the boxes that apply -->\n\n- [ ] My code follows the code style of this project\n- [ ] I have updated the documentation accordingly\n- [ ] I have added tests to cover my changes\n- [ ] All new and existing tests passed\n- [ ] I have updated CHANGELOG.md\n- [ ] My changes generate no new linter warnings\n- [ ] I have checked my code for security issues\n\n## Screenshots (if applicable)\n\n<!-- Add screenshots to help explain your changes -->\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n<!-- Any additional information that reviewers should know -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5W7fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn1kQAGtPDjfqSY4gTF+G6H+dYFN4\nDV5WkoYQyVPyopsEQY2touT0lRZwLIFUEGhamgfHEYKYt8s2MghpgoGVO8LeU4X0\nk/MrP5v+NEyAruT+VGfO8INYvgKJanwp6dUGo9nh/1qXCJ5HdhfFou5iT75UkUGJ\nE43Z8mDlRd+zdjDkv5MS4LrMbDL0uhUXWbyQigaC1PSU5vpe+E0gKnuYcD2lXo9I\ntiumY0A6yV+tpdCE8VHvRCQJCqtEHxaHVBzfTUsc3YpeZJkhtDY5bCxelCNpfOS1\nd5AaQLX3oBx/HAee116TyQT8Ium8mFbrBn/fikTxcFV+kntc4WOI6bBBtczgaE7L\nSIgGAbG6n7NkmI5006VvXGXDmIoxzLiWf8AJNN/9MCElTXaQWedCGYT6H/tkhUoK\n/EPwKEP/efLD5ai/jlt1KpX9VKeP228uf4gFfz94UrjX1UISjKZc/kaBBfG6U6nM\nk/UgTOmf5098bePt2qOcfof3qZlxlXUIRvmjEA1ka1v1QX6o/35NLZNHR/sIAADg\nvDAwO080tTF9zWaFHmnkw6ta66z1Moe4jkz8+S7QzjUC16VVpoW91z8xeEgyy+8i\nZ+WS4YxE1TVXaS5Zj5vjTCqerdyg6TBw8bpO8oBbBLtkBO/yrM2XsY0vsx3ZuRvA\ncaJsquE6FyZMXd1BPp44\n=WcUn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-20T00:10:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","