tps://api.github.com/users/anwarika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anwarika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anwarika/spark-engine/commits/8ad36a29ef85636b8dff022db7f60397df342fa2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-01T23:41:05Z","email":"kani.anwari@gmail.com","name":"Kanishkah Anwari"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-01T23:41:05Z","email":"kani.anwari@gmail.com","name":"Kanishkah Anwari"},"message":"fix(hallucinations): 5-layer defence against LLM field invention\n\nFix 1 — Inject full data schema into every edit prompt\n  LLMService._EDIT_PROMPT_TEMPLATE now includes <<<DATA_SCHEMA>>>\n  populated from the same MOCK DATA AVAILABLE block used for new\n  generation so the LLM sees exact snake_case field names.\n\nFix 2 — temperature=0.15 for edits (was gateway default ~0.7)\n  Deterministic edits reduce creative field invention.\n\nFix 3 — Anchor to fields already present in the existing code\n  _extract_existing_fields() scans apiData() access patterns and\n  injects them as \"safe to reuse\" hints in the edit prompt.\n\nFix 4 — Auto-retry (up to 2 attempts) with error context fed back\n  _generate_edit_with_retry() in chat.py runs validate+compile;\n  on failure it re-calls generate_edit_response(prior_error=...)\n  so the LLM sees what went wrong and self-corrects.\n  Both /message and /message/stream use this helper.\n\nFix 5 — Schema field contract check in CodeValidator\n  _check_data_field_contract() extracts all apiData().X accesses\n  and rejects any X not in _ALL_VALID_FIELDS (union of all profile\n  top-level keys). Treats violations as hard errors so the retry\n  loop catches them before the iframe ever renders.\n  e.g. apiData().totalRevenue → validation error → retry → fixed.\n\nMade-with: Cursor","tree":{"sha":"de8ce00bb1f4227ad9e998a3f681fb68f139e50e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anwarika/spark-engine/git/trees/de8ce00bb1f4227ad9e998a3f681fb68f1